iew_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commit/a4eb920261b52986ab6acd2ac6bdc937a5b7d7bd","node_id":"C_kwDOSD2bxdoAKGE0ZWI5MjAyNjFiNTI5ODZhYjZhY2QyYWM2YmRjOTM3YTViN2Q3YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commit/0272b0872e1b9a0b1edba579a653c43a02096d26","sha":"0272b0872e1b9a0b1edba579a653c43a02096d26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commits/0272b0872e1b9a0b1edba579a653c43a02096d26"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commit/b974b774856869f2f741de43a11506c7690b9cc0","sha":"b974b774856869f2f741de43a11506c7690b9cc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commits/b974b774856869f2f741de43a11506c7690b9cc0"}],"sha":"a4eb920261b52986ab6acd2ac6bdc937a5b7d7bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commits/a4eb920261b52986ab6acd2ac6bdc937a5b7d7bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/8329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel","id":35613825,"login":"vercel[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MzU2MTM4MjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/commits/b974b774856869f2f741de43a11506c7690b9cc0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-05T23:33:30Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-05T23:33:30Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"message":"Update repository for React Flight RCE advisory\n\n# React Flight / Next.js RCE Advisory (CVE-2025-66478) - Security Patch\n\n## Summary\nSuccessfully applied security patches to address the critical React Flight / Next.js RCE vulnerability (CVE-2025-66478) in the ai-sdk-computer-use repository.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### Files Modified\n1. **package.json** - Updated dependency versions\n   - `react`: `^19.0.0` → `^19.0.1` (vulnerable to patched version)\n   - `react-dom`: `^19.0.0` → `^19.0.1` (vulnerable to patched version)\n   - `next`: `15.2.1` → `15.2.6` (vulnerable to patched version)\n   - `eslint-config-next`: `15.2.1` → `15.2.6` (for consistency)\n\n2. **pnpm-lock.yaml** - Updated lockfile to resolve patched dependencies\n   - `react`: `19.0.0` → `19.2.1` (resolved from ^19.0.1)\n   - `react-dom`: `19.0.0` → `19.2.1` (resolved from ^19.0.1)\n   - All other dependencies updated to compatible versions\n\n## Vulnerability Details\nThe project was affected by the critical RCE vulnerability in React Server Components that allows arbitrary code execution through the React Flight protocol. The vulnerability affected:\n- React 19.0.0 (vulnerable version)\n- Next.js 15.2.x < 15.2.6 (vulnerable versions)\n\n## Patched Versions Applied\nAccording to the official GitHub security advisory (GHSA-9qr9-h5gf-34mp):\n- **Next.js 15.2.x**: Upgraded to `15.2.6` (patched version)\n- **React 19.0.x**: Updated to satisfy `^19.0.1`, resolved to `19.2.1` (a more recent patched version)\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### Detection Process\n1. Scanned package.json files (monorepo-aware)\n2. Identified Next.js dependency at 15.2.1 (vulnerable)\n3. Identified React 19.0.0 (vulnerable) and React-dom 19.0.0 (vulnerable)\n4. Confirmed no React Flight/RSC packages present (react-server-dom-*)\n\n### Patching Strategy\nSince the project uses Next.js (not a standalone React Flight app):\n- Did NOT manually update react/react-dom to specific versions\n- Instead, updated package.json constraints to `^19.0.1`\n- Let `pnpm install` resolve to the best compatible versions\n- Result: Resolved to React 19.2.1, which is a patched version\n\n### Build Verification\n✅ Successfully ran `npm run build` (next build)\n✅ Build completed without errors\n✅ All pages generated correctly\n✅ No breaking changes introduced\n\n## Verification Results\n\n**Lockfile Resolution:**\n```\nreact: ^19.0.1 → resolved to 19.2.1 ✓\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1 → resolved to 19.2.1 ✓\nnext: 15.2.6 ✓ (patched version from 15.2.1)\n```\n\n**Build Status:**\n```\n✓ Compiled successfully\n✓ Type checking passed\n✓ Generated all static pages (9/9)\n✓ Build completed successfully\n```\n\n## Impact Assessment\n- ✅ Security vulnerability addressed\n- ✅ No breaking changes to application logic\n- ✅ All dependencies remain within compatible ranges\n- ✅ Build passes without errors\n- ✅ No React Flight packages in use (simple Next.js app with RSC)\n\n## Notes\n- The project''s Next.js configuration already had the patched version in the lockfile (15.2.6), but package.json was pinned to 15.2.1\n- Running `pnpm install` after updating React ensured all versions resolved correctly\n- This is a standard Next.js application using React Server Components, not a standalone React Flight app\n- React was updated to 19.2.1 which is a more recent patched version than the minimum required 19.0.1\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a9d084c3bac122816760a759ecc13d8cc0d02c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junjiemeng01/ai-sdk-computer-use/git/trees/7a9d084c3bac122816760a759ecc13d8cc0d02c5"},"url":"https://api.githu