theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/267dca881f4ce5881b10639b7a600162ed23a10d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T02:35:25Z","email":"kanav11dwevedi@gmail.com","name":"KDwevedi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T02:35:25Z","email":"kanav11dwevedi@gmail.com","name":"KDwevedi"},"message":"fix(pgr): remove duplicate sub-type on complaint summary page\n\nThe Complaint Summary page rendered the complaint sub-type label twice:\nonce as a grey chip next to the \"Complaint Details\" section title\n(serviceTitle, derived from serviceCode -> SERVICEDEFS.<code>) and again\nas the dedicated \"Complaint Sub Type\" detail row (same SERVICEDEFS.<code>\nvalue). Removed the redundant header chip; the sub-type still shows via\nits own labeled row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8255341117bd3d9ee6f8020ed286667a099290d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/8255341117bd3d9ee6f8020ed286667a099290d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/267dca881f4ce5881b10639b7a600162ed23a10d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74085496?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KDwevedi","id":74085496,"login":"KDwevedi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MDg1NDk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/267dca881f4ce5881b10639b7a600162ed23a10d","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDI2N2RjYTg4MWY0Y2U1ODgxYjEwNjM5YjdhNjAwMTYyZWQyM2ExMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108","sha":"3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108"}],"sha":"267dca881f4ce5881b10639b7a600162ed23a10d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/267dca881f4ce5881b10639b7a600162ed23a10d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74085496?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KDwevedi","id":74085496,"login":"KDwevedi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MDg1NDk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T09:55:24Z","email":"74085496+KDwevedi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kanav Dwevedi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T09:55:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pgr): make map ward-highlight colour MDMS-configurable (#119)\n\nThe complaint-location map''s ward highlight was a hardcoded\n`#FFA74F` orange in two components (GeoLocations — the create-flow\n\"Pin Complaint Location\" step — and ComplaintLocationMap — the detail\nview). Operators had no way to theme it per tenant.\n\n- New shared hook `useWardHighlightColor` reads\n  `RAINMAKER-PGR.MapConfig[0].wardHighlightColor` from MDMS (tenant\n  from CITIZEN.COMMON.HOME.CITY / getCurrentTenantId), validates it''s\n  a hex, and falls back to the legacy `#FFA74F` while loading, when\n  the master is absent, on error, or on a bad value — so any tenant\n  without a MapConfig record keeps the exact original behaviour.\n- Both components consume the hook; `wardStyleFor` now takes the\n  colour as a parameter instead of a module constant.\n\nDefault unchanged (#FFA74F). Bomet seeds MapConfig with the navy\nheader colour (#22394D) at tenant `ke`.\n\nFOLLOW-UP: expose wardHighlightColor (and broader map theming) in the\nDIGIT Studio configurator so operators set it from the UI instead of\nseeding MDMS by hand — noted in the hook and tracked as an issue.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76a34d752abda635582f80d3a5a2826bcc6b4cf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/76a34d752abda635582f80d3a5a2826bcc6b4cf5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108","verification":{"payload":"tree 76a34d752abda635582f80d3a5a2826bcc6b4cf5\nparent e7120efe058ab94d8cb808fda11e784a88b16862\nauthor Kanav Dwevedi <74085496+KDwevedi@users.noreply.github.com> 1778925324 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778925324 +0530\n\nfeat(pgr): make map ward-highlight colour MDMS-configurable (#119)\n\nThe complaint-location map''s ward highlight was a hardcoded\n`#FFA74F` orange in two components (GeoLocations — the create-flow\n\"Pin Complaint Location\" step — and ComplaintLocationMap — the detail\nview). Operators had no way to theme it per tenant.\n\n- New shared hook `useWardHighlightColor` reads\n  `RAINMAKER-PGR.MapConfig[0].wardHighlightColor` from MDMS (tenant\n  from CITIZEN.COMMON.HOME.CITY / getCurrentTenantId), validates it''s\n  a hex, and falls back to the legacy `#FFA74F` while loading, when\n  the master is absent, on error, or on a bad value — so any tenant\n  without a MapConfig record keeps the exact original behaviour.\n- Both components consume the hook; `wardStyleFor` now takes the\n  colour as a parameter instead of a module constant.\n\nDefault unchanged (#FFA74F). Bomet seeds MapConfig with the navy\nheader colour (#22394D) at tenant `ke`.\n\nFOLLOW-UP: expose wardHighlightColor (and broader map theming) in the\nDIGIT Studio configurator so operators set it from the UI instead of\nseeding MDMS by hand — noted in the hook and tracked as an issue.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCD8MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjMEQADHQlnaWPOaossS5j6Tkz4DL\nsRUYde3BDBCV6mn/okwMtzork7o6xnpyXVJcZ56lifAJA6iEV5pwbXHs/gUZ7lBB\naiSPNECdkqJ+LQ4GTY+STFLAcD9MqJ0OsVRbONgA4qyrbqwwTAyvujFIFsceeMTG\nGhEsO6yfML4H1bIwTqJJBxI9Etd9tSin8aqLzmJyPQBL1a/Tyz5nrmcbLDq6csCn\nbEkePCAvNQAJ7cbZPcuQXUfnRfKQnr5ujbmTL+Lfd4EMeYoq37gPxbm91Rmn/U/E\nAeDkdDxqCvHhQk3fGa3bXxsQ6VJj7j6Ybp1BGZxWMyUKd0fNnnczFEa4gChw5AeT\nTTxOQtEUAT1UhMYztEEVOCYR3UV7HYlLrX1IhIguJpUI3oG1xQkO5Icb646Jj/Bc\nTQQNRucDJ7znBE7U+6XU3oR+0mIViHe53Z4oWRki4d9oNcLZqu30EFm19uQPUNB0\n5Lm+7SAcniNflZ2XlPaiUZ0fdEY1Jc40mf+W5mtSIyPFkiJr1mOAVi4FmD7a8aiE\ndYCRfCKc/nihyBhCyb5+rrMd6EP0yiX0/XZ04ITNspUsf9gACOfCb3y+ev2M9ZE6\nBV7Ujpe6Fl2eQ+WB72Y3vi6PUtKyAog4nP8mCNhevh3XxEIriS3hIbijXjnmBR/l\nPYY8C9rQEQeGvkR2cieR\n=vyj2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-16T09:55:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDM1OTRhMWNlNWQwYmZjZDI4ODNmYWNkMGI0MjJhMzEyMzU4MGUxMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e7120efe058ab94d8cb808fda11e784a88b16862","sha":"e7120efe058ab94d8cb808fda11e784a88b16862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e7120efe058ab94d8cb808fda11e784a88b16862"}],"sha":"3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/3594a1ce5d0bfcd2883facd0b422a3123580e108"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74085496?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KDwevedi","id":74085496,"login":"KDwevedi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MDg1NDk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KDwevedi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e7120efe058ab94d8cb808fda11e784a88b16862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T08:51:18Z","email":"74085496+KDwevedi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kanav Dwevedi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T08:51:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pgr): redo CCRS #524 / #489 / #490 against products/pgr (the live tree) (#118)\n\nPRs #112, #114, #116 each merged + deployed against\n`packages/modules/pgr/...` and `packages/react-components/atoms/...`,\nbut those files aren''t in the live bundle. `esbuild.dev.js` and\n`esbuild.build.js` both alias `@egovernments/digit-ui-module-pgr` to\n`products/pgr/src/Module.js`, so the PGR import resolves entirely\ninside `products/pgr/`. The `packages/modules/pgr/` tree is orphan\ncode from the bundler''s perspective. Story 5.18 caught it on naipepea\nQA: the employee timeline was still rendering the raw 8-role string\nthat #112 thought it had stripped.\n\nThis PR redoes all three fixes against the right tree, on top of the\nexisting CCRS-specific layout (TimeLineWrapper, TimeLine, and the\nalready-correct pendingAtLme.js — the prefix issue is patched in\nTimeLine.js:106 with `text=\"\"`).\n\nproducts/pgr/src/components/TimeLineWrapper.js (employee timeline,\nimported by PGRDetails.js):\n\n- CCRS#524 — drop the `formatPerson` role concat. The wall-of-text on\n  admin rows (\"Nairobi Admin - Customer Support Representative,\n  Grievance Routing Officer, ACCESSCONTROL_ROLES_ROLES_SUPERUSER,\n  Workbench MDMS Admin, HRMS ADMIN, Complaint Viewer, Employee, CCRS\n  Last Mile Employee\") is built locally here from `person.roles`,\n  not appended by egov-workflow-v2 as #112 assumed. Just return\n  `person.name`; the row label already describes the action.\n\n- CCRS#490 sub-bugs 2-4 — extend `isAssigningAction` to include\n  `ESCALATE`, so auto-escalator rows surface the new-level LME instead\n  of the actor who originally clicked Assign. Add a `CS_NA` fallback\n  so a missing assignee renders \"NA\" instead of dropping the row\n  caption.\n\n- CCRS#489 — parse the `[CODE]` prefix on `instance.comment`. When the\n  code resolves to a known `CS_REJECTION__<CODE>` localization key,\n  show \"Rejection Reason: <label>\" with any trailing free text after\n  an em-dash. Falls back to the existing \"Employee Comments: \\\"...\\\"\"\n  framing for non-reject comments so other audit messages render\n  identically.\n\nproducts/pgr/src/components/TimeLine.js (citizen timeline, imported\nby pages/citizen/ComplaintDetails.js):\n\n- CCRS#489 — same `[CODE]` parse, extracted as a small `TLCommentItem`\n  helper so the existing `comment?.map` site stays a one-liner. Falls\n  back to `WF_COMMON_COMMENTS` heading when the code doesn''t resolve\n  (so other modules sharing this code path are untouched). Citizen\n  workflow doesn''t enrich `assigner.name` with roles, so #524''s\n  concern doesn''t apply on this side.\n\n`products/pgr/src/components/timelineInstances/pendingAtLme.js` was\nalready correct — `text` is an optional prefix, and TimeLine.js:106\nalready passes `\"\"`. No change needed; PR #116''s pendingAtLme delta\nduplicated work this tree had done.\n\nRefs egovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#524,\negovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#489,\negovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#490.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"875a856b551f06b844d09ef27eb993ea802cb062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/875a856b551f06b844d09ef27eb993ea802cb062"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/e7120efe058ab94d8cb808fda11e784a88b16862","verification":{"payload":"tree 875a856b551f06b844d09ef27eb993ea802cb062\nparent f4ef813df06ff0d4547dcac7dce442e5447d9f72\nauthor Kanav Dwevedi <74085496+KDwevedi@users.noreply.github.com> 1778748678 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778748678 +0530\n\nfix(pgr): redo CCRS #524 / #489 / #490 against products/pgr (the live tree) (#118)\n\nPRs #112, #114, #116 each merged + deployed against\n`packages/modules/pgr/...` and `packages/react-components/atoms/...`,\nbut those files aren''t in the live bundle. `esbuild.dev.js` and\n`esbuild.build.js` both alias `@egovernments/digit-ui-module-pgr` to\n`products/pgr/src/Module.js`, so the PGR import resolves entirely\ninside `products/pgr/`. The `packages/modules/pgr/` tree is orphan\ncode from the bundler''s perspective. Story 5.18 caught it on naipepea\nQA: the employee timeline was still rendering the raw 8-role string\nthat #112 thought it had stripped.\n\nThis PR redoes all three fixes against the right tree, on top of the\nexisting CCRS-specific layout (TimeLineWrapper, TimeLine, and the\nalready-correct pendingAtLme.js — the prefix issue is patched in\nTimeLine.js:106 with `text=\"\"`).\n\nproducts/pgr/src/components/TimeLineWrapper.js (employee timeline,\nimported by PGRDetails.js):\n\n- CCRS#524 — drop the `formatPerson` role concat. The wall-of-text on\n  admin rows (\"Nairobi Admin - Customer Support Representative,\n  Grievance Routing Officer, ACCESSCONTROL_ROLES_ROLES_SUPERUSER,\n  Workbench MDMS Admin, HRMS ADMIN, Complaint Viewer, Employee, CCRS\n  Last Mile Employee\") is built locally here from `person.roles`,\n  not appended by egov-workflow-v2 as #112 assumed. Just return\n  `person.name`; the row label already describes the action.\n\n- CCRS#490 sub-bugs 2-4 — extend `isAssigningAction` to include\n  `ESCALATE`, so auto-escalator rows surface the new-level LME instead\n  of the actor who originally clicked Assign. Add a `CS_NA` fallback\n  so a missing assignee renders \"NA\" instead of dropping the row\n  caption.\n\n- CCRS#489 — parse the `[CODE]` prefix on `instance.comment`. When the\n  code resolves to a known `CS_REJECTION__<CODE>` localization key,\n  show \"Rejection Reason: <label>\" with any trailing free text after\n  an em-dash. Falls back to the existing \"Employee Comments: \\\"...\\\"\"\n  framing for non-reject comments so other audit messages render\n  identically.\n\nproducts/pgr/src/components/TimeLine.js (citizen timeline, imported\nby pages/citizen/ComplaintDetails.js):\n\n- CCRS#489 — same `[CODE]` parse, extracted as a small `TLCommentItem`\n  helper so the existing `comment?.map` site stays a one-liner. Falls\n  back to `WF_COMMON_COMMENTS` heading when the code doesn''t resolve\n  (so other modules sharing this code path are untouched). Citizen\n  workflow doesn''t enrich `assigner.name` with roles, so #524''s\n  concern doesn''t apply on this side.\n\n`products/pgr/src/components/timelineInstances/pendingAtLme.js` was\nalready correct — `text` is an optional prefix, and TimeLine.js:106\nalready passes `\"\"`. No change needed; PR #116''s pendingAtLme delta\nduplicated work this tree had done.\n\nRefs egovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#524,\negovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#489,\negovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#490.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBY0GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvysQAJtgxB4sjpzpmNmbd50igdWr\nGvFHnorSc1Ds8A9HpNQEcGDaF1WEVdvTR4K0M6Fu8Wi5YiIGm9z/8ThayxoVG3nE\nhs0Njz07O