47?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/5fc655c9a3ade0a67c7e8cdb9f3e1eafe49e9394","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDVmYzY1NWM5YTNhZGUwYTY3YzdlOGNkYjlmM2UxZWFmZTQ5ZTkzOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e946d4f7e4cfe4b67c30dadb364e00816aa9757e","sha":"e946d4f7e4cfe4b67c30dadb364e00816aa9757e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e946d4f7e4cfe4b67c30dadb364e00816aa9757e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e61d1b17b9d5a686f98613c338f1b932d57a9087","sha":"e61d1b17b9d5a686f98613c338f1b932d57a9087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e61d1b17b9d5a686f98613c338f1b932d57a9087"}],"sha":"5fc655c9a3ade0a67c7e8cdb9f3e1eafe49e9394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5fc655c9a3ade0a67c7e8cdb9f3e1eafe49e9394"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e61d1b17b9d5a686f98613c338f1b932d57a9087/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T10:33:03Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T10:33:03Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(naipepea): stop PGR inbox auto-refetch after search submit\n\nCCRS#558. The Employee CMS inbox refreshed back to its unfiltered\nstate immediately after the operator typed a complaint id and hit\nSearch — the just-fetched filtered result was overwritten in-place\nby the default inbox query. Two stacked causes:\n\n1. `PGRInbox.js` reassigned `updatedConfig` *outside* the `useMemo`\n   that produces it. Lines 143-178 ran an additional spread —\n   `updatedConfig = { ...updatedConfig, sections: {…} }` — on every\n   render to inject mobile-validation rules a second time. The same\n   injection already happens up-front against `configs`, which is\n   then deep-cloned into `pageConfig` (the useMemo''s actual input),\n   so the second pass was pure dead weight that happened to break\n   reference stability on the prop passed to `<InboxSearchComposer/>`.\n\n2. `InboxSearchComposer` (`packages/digit-ui-components/src/hoc/`)\n   had a cleanup-on-unmount effect whose deps array was `[configs]`\n   instead of `[]`. The comment above it already said \"when the\n   component unmounts,\" but React fires the cleanup on *every* deps\n   change, not only on unmount. Combined with (1), every render\n   tripped the cleanup, which `clearSessionFormData()`''d the search\n   state, reset the search/filter forms to their default values,\n   and the downstream data-fetch effect promptly refetched with\n   those defaults — visible as the inbox \"snapping back\" to the\n   unfiltered list right after the search response arrived.\n\nFixes:\n\n- PGRInbox.js: drop the post-`useMemo` reassignment (the\n  duplicate mobile-validation injection) and the two leftover\n  `console.log(\"*** Log ===> …\")` debug prints. The first\n  injection at lines 66-100 is sufficient — it mutates `configs`\n  before the location effect deep-clones it into `pageConfig`.\n- InboxSearchComposer.js: pin the cleanup deps to `[]` so the\n  effect only fires on real unmount, matching its existing\n  comment. The cleanup still needs to read the latest `configs`\n  defaults to know what to reset to, so it now reads them through\n  a ref (`cleanupConfigsRef`) that''s updated by a sibling effect\n  on every render. This is the standard \"stale-closure-safe\n  unmount cleanup\" pattern.\n\nVerified locally as employee against the naipepea Kong tunnel:\nloaded /digit-ui/employee/pgr/inbox-v2, instrumented network\ncapture, typed `PGR-TEST-12345` into the complaint-number field,\nclicked Search. Exactly two `/pgr-services/v2/request/_search`\nrequests fired across the whole session — one initial load\n(no `serviceRequestId`), one after Search (with\n`serviceRequestId=PGR-TEST-12345`). Waited 5+ seconds after the\nfiltered request; no follow-up refetch. The search input retained\nthe typed value and the table correctly showed zero rows for the\nfake id.\n\nBefore this fix the same sequence produced a 3rd request\nimmediately after the filtered one (with the default\n`PENDINGFORASSIGNMENT` etc. statuses but no `serviceRequestId`),\nwhich is what the operator perceived as \"the inbox refreshes\nautomatically\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"261a988628211ac65b0a0623dee37878e9385aa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/261a988628211ac65b0a0623dee37878e9385aa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/e61d1b17b9d5a686f98613c338f1b932d57a9087","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e61d1b17b9d5a686f98613c338f1b932d57a9087","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGU2MWQxYjE3YjlkNWE2ODZmOTg2MTNjMzM4ZjFiOTMyZDU3YTkwODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e946d4f7e4cfe4b67c30dadb364e00816aa9757e","sha":"e946d