abf8292b48285e4aae970baeb9d53e4ea1ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/a1efabf8292b48285e4aae970baeb9d53e4ea1ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/09057c991b580d909c86e2976080302611f24e08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T09:55:41Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T09:55:41Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(naipepea): unbreak Update Password from Edit Profile\n\nCCRS follow-up. Gurjeet reported that the Update Password affordance\non the Edit Profile page doesn''t work. Reproduced for both citizens\nand employees on naipepea. Two stacked bugs explain it:\n\n1. `setUserCurrentPassword` (UserProfile.js:455) ran the validity\n   check but **never called `setCurrentPassword(value)`** — so the\n   typed value never reached state. The save handler''s gate\n   `currentPassword.length && newPassword.length && confirmPassword.length`\n   was therefore always false (current stayed \"\"), the change-password\n   branch never fired, and `/user/password/_update` was never called.\n   This silently broke the flow for *every* user. The sibling\n   handlers (`setUserNewPassword`, `setUserConfirmPassword`) already\n   call their state setters; mirror that here.\n\n2. Once #1 is fixed, the citizen flow still fails — the payload\n   hardcoded `type: \"EMPLOYEE\"` (UserProfile.js:650). The user service\n   uses `type` to scope the username lookup, so a citizen hitting\n   the endpoint got `UserNotFoundException: User not found for given\n   criteria … type=EMPLOYEE`. Derive `type` from the `userType` prop\n   the route already passes in (\"citizen\" from /citizen/user/profile,\n   \"employee\" from /employee/user/profile) so the lookup runs against\n   the correct user table on both sides.\n\nVerified against naipepea Kong:\n- `/user/password/_update` with `type=EMPLOYEE` for citizen Dennis\n  returned `UserNotFoundException`.\n- Same request with `type=CITIZEN` returned `PasswordMismatchException`\n  for the (intentional) wrong existing password — i.e. user resolved\n  correctly, validator rejected the wrong password as expected. With\n  the correct current password this path would persist a new password.\n- Same request with `type=EMPLOYEE` for ADMIN (real employee)\n  returned `PasswordMismatchException` — confirming the employee\n  side of the type check was already fine; it''s just the citizen\n  side that was broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ffe55af13424e6a0e2a3174706b38786fbd924e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/4ffe55af13424e6a0e2a3174706b38786fbd924e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/09057c991b580d909c86e2976080302611f24e08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/09057c991b580d909c86e2976080302611f24e08","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDA5MDU3Yzk5MWI1ODBkOTA5Yzg2ZTI5NzYwODAzMDI2MTFmMjRlMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/53ef606d8061dd1cf701eb4d1136142440dc79be","sha":"53ef606d8061dd1cf701eb4d1136142440dc79be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/53ef606d8061dd1cf701eb4d1136142440dc79be"}],"sha":"09057c991b580d909c86e2976080302611f24e08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/09057c991b580d909c86e2976080302611f24e08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"