c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/8e729536a6ddf509ea5ac26ac2d4892b1b038657","sha":"8e729536a6ddf509ea5ac26ac2d4892b1b038657","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/8e729536a6ddf509ea5ac26ac2d4892b1b038657"}],"sha":"82f706ea95f5718f9758dbc438b455bdd8fe01bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/82f706ea95f5718f9758dbc438b455bdd8fe01bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/8e729536a6ddf509ea5ac26ac2d4892b1b038657/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T09:10:38Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T09:10:38Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(ccrs): hide HRMS from employee UI — managed via configurator\n\nCCRS#561. The employee home page rendered an HRMS card for any user\nholding HRMS_ADMIN. Per product direction, HRMS is managed from the\nseparate /configurator/ app, not from inside digit-ui — even users\nwith HRMS roles should access those APIs via configurator.\n\nTwo coordinated changes:\n\n1. `src/App.js` — drop the HRMS module from the boot sequence:\n   - Remove the `@egovernments/digit-ui-module-hrms` import.\n   - Remove `\"HRMS\"` from `enabledModules`, so the modules array\n     fetched from `digitInitData` filters HRMS out → EmployeeHome''s\n     `modules?.map(({code}) => <{code}Card />)` never renders an\n     `<HRMSCard />`.\n   - Remove `initHRMSComponents()` so HRMS hooks/components never\n     register and `/digit-ui/employee/hrms/*` routes don''t mount.\n\n2. `packages/modules/workbench/src/Module.js` — defense-in-depth:\n   - Drop the `HRMSCard` import.\n   - Register `HRMSCard: null` (matching the existing `DSSCard: null`\n     pattern). So even if a future change re-adds HRMS to\n     `enabledModules` by mistake, the home card stays hidden.\n\nVerified locally on http://localhost:18080/digit-ui/employee/ against\nthe naipepea Kong tunnel: signed in as ADMIN (HRMS_ADMIN role present),\nhome shows exactly two cards — \"Citizen Complaint Resolution System\"\nand \"Workbench\". No HRMS text anywhere on the page. `/hrms/*` URLs\nwill land in the not-found redirect set by AppModules since no route\nis registered.\n\nSidebar entries for HRMS (driven by access-control MDMS, not by\n`enabledModules`) will keep showing until tenants add `\"HRMS\"` to\n`EMPLOYEE_MODULE_DENYLIST` in their `globalConfigs.js`. That''s a\ndeploy-side change handled per-tenant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cf85ab6234a35d4bc42e415a391b4150ab46e1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/5cf85ab6234a35d4bc42e415a391b4150ab46e1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/8e729536a6ddf509ea5ac26ac2d4892b1b038657","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"veri