ub.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/477255e871dbe2db0198de63372a5ceeb0485c8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T12:20:34Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T12:20:34Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): manage-master-data search input double border\n\nThe Workbench manage-master-data search uses a `.text-input`\nwrapper (not the `.digit-text-input-field` variant) with an inner\n`.employee-card-input` (no `digit-` prefix, hyphen instead of\ncamelCase). The wrapper picked up the unified 1px / 6px chrome,\nthe inner input picked up the same from\n`input[type=\"text\"]:not(...)` — visible double border around the\nsearch field.\n\nTreat `.text-input` and `.text-input.mdms-search-input` as canonical\nwrappers (flex / overflow:hidden / white bg, no padding), and strip\nthe inner input''s chrome like the existing\n`.digit-text-input-field input.digit-employeeCard-input` rule does.\nAlso added `.employee-card-input` to its own block matching the\ncamelCase variant''s surface chrome so standalone usages stay\nconsistent with everything else.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b686e0e59e98180a03cd8428261c7b566d5c62e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/b686e0e59e98180a03cd8428261c7b566d5c62e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/477255e871dbe2db0198de63372a5ceeb0485c8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"com