r","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/7ec8868aad8be0a44fcd5d0b99b82a6b13f689ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:54:36Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:54:36Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): strip hover shadow from rating-star buttons\n\nHovering a star on /citizen/pgr/rate picked up the vendor button\nhover shadow (.v2-scope cascade). Star buttons are icon-only\naffordances — the only feedback should be the icon''s color/fill\nflipping to brand yellow. Reset every interactive state on\n.v2-rating-star to transparent / no-shadow / no-outline so the\nframe stays invisible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fbc730f5854a51177688fa34689ed4949af2584","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/2fbc730f5854a51177688fa34689ed4949af2584"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/7ec8868aad8be0a44fcd5d0b99b82a6b13f689ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/7ec8868aad8be0a44fcd5d0b99b82a6b13f689ef","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDdlYzg4NjhhYWQ4YmUwYTQ0ZmNkNWQwYjk5YjgyYTZiMTNmNjg5ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da","sha":"f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da"}],"sha":"7ec8868aad8be0a44fcd5d0b99b82a6b13f689ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/7ec8868aad8be0a44fcd5d0b99b82a6b13f689ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:53:52Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:53:52Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"feat(modernize): citizen rate page (/citizen/pgr/rate/:id)\n\nThe vendor RatingCard was the last citizen surface still rendering\nthe legacy chrome — modernised it inline using v2 primitives.\n\n- Header + sub-text via ScreenHeader (matches the rest of the\n  citizen flow''s voice)\n- StarRow: 5 lucide Star buttons with brand-tinted fill + hover\n  preview. Replaces the legacy <Rating /> from\n  digit-ui-react-components.\n- FeedbackCheckbox: native input with brand `accent-color`,\n  arranged in a 2-col grid; fits the form rhythm of the rest of v2.\n- v2 Textarea for comments, v2 Button (yellow CTA, dark text) for\n  submit.\n\nWiring untouched — same `useComplaintDetails` lookup, same\n`updateComplaints` dispatch, same await-then-redirect into\n/response so the redux slice lands before Response.js mounts\n(CCRS#473). The CS_FEEDBACK_WHAT_WAS_GOOD undefined-array guard\nfrom CCRS#441 is preserved by always running picks through a\nfilter map.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f9dab3ef079226e00a57bd9293e60a48dccebcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/5f9dab3ef079226e00a57bd9293e60a48dccebcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGYwMzJlMmQ4NzdlYzg5MTFkZTZkM2QwY2MxNWNmZjk5YTdiYTE0ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f","sha":"5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f"}],"sha":"f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/f032e2d877ec8911de6d3d0cc15cff99a7ba14da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:50:13Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:50:13Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"revert(pgr): drop ward auto-fill debug + matcher broadening\n\nUser confirmed the step-reduction (6 → 5 steps with the combined\nlocation step) is good enough progress; the County auto-fill miss\non naipepea is a data-side issue (the bundled wards GeoJSON''s hint\ncodes don''t align with the MDMS boundary tree''s ward codes / names)\nand not worth chasing further from the UI.\n\nReverts:\n- The temporary `[BoundaryComponent] auto-fill` console.log + leaf\n  sampler. Console stays clean.\n- The matcher broadening (name field check, substring fallback,\n  case-insensitive boundaryType). `findWardPath` is back to the\n  original strict (exact / `_<hint>` suffix) match against the\n  ward''s `code` field. When the GeoJSON hint doesn''t match, the\n  cascade simply stays empty and the user picks manually — same\n  behaviour the citizen flow has had since CCRS#491.\n\nKept (these are not part of the prefilling trial):\n- `autoFilledKeys` tracking so a manually-picked level doesn''t\n  re-disable itself after the user clicks it.\n- `readOnly` prop on BoundaryComponent / BoundaryDropdown so the\n  combined location step can render the auto-filled cascade as\n  read-only when it does succeed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"455152af52f6513862d00e39e33c3c85376f65e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/455152af52f6513862d00e39e33c3c85376f65e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDU0NDE0OTNiNDAzZDM1OTg0ZjcxN2UxYjg0ODlhZWY0Yzk0Y2NhMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e","sha":"e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e"}],"sha":"5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5441493b403d35984f717e1b8489aef4c94cca0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:46:42Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:46:42Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"debug(pgr): dump leaf samples + case-insensitive Ward type check\n\nEven the lenient substring matcher missed `Ngara`, so either the\ntree''s leaf-type isn''t `Ward` (case mismatch) or the GeoJSON ward\ngenuinely isn''t in the MDMS tree. Two adjustments:\n\n1. Match on `String(boundaryType).toUpperCase() === ''WARD''` so\n   `WARD` / `ward` / `Ward` all qualify.\n\n2. Expanded the auto-fill console log to also dump up to 8 leaf\n   nodes from the boundary tree (their depth, type, code, name).\n   Tells us at a glance whether wards exist at all in the tree\n   under what type, what their codes/names look like, and where the\n   hint is failing to align.\n\nBoth kept temporary while we pin down naipepea''s tree shape; will\nstrip after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"787a560d5b36e5e083287b7b313b2a503aaa8a34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/787a560d5b36e5e083287b7b313b2a503aaa8a34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGUzOGEwZWEzMDdkM2MyYzZlM2JjYTI2MmYxMTE3OTMyZWEyOTY0OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c","sha":"028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c"}],"sha":"e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e38a0ea307d3c2c6e3bca262f1117932ea29648e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:43:45Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:43:45Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(pgr): zoom-out map default + broaden ward path matcher\n\n- Map default zoom drops from 15 (street level) to 13 (neighborhood\n  / district). Citizens land on a frame that shows surrounding area\n  instead of a single block, while still close enough that a tap\n  meaningfully picks a routable point. Centralised the constant\n  (DEFAULT_ZOOM) and applied it everywhere `setView` was hardcoded\n  to 15. The no-GPS fallback (zoom 5, country level) is unchanged.\n\n- Broaden findWardPath matcher. The previous version only checked\n  the boundary node''s `code` (exact / suffix); naipepea''s ward codes\n  don''t end with the GeoJSON''s bare hint (e.g. live tree codes like\n  `Kilimani` or `ke.nairobi.kilimani` against a GeoJSON\n  `KILIMANI`), so the auto-fill silently fell through and the user\n  saw a blank County / Sub-County / Ward cascade after pinning the\n  map.\n\n  Now matches both code AND name fields, in two passes:\n    1. Strict — exact or `_<hint>` suffix\n    2. Lenient — substring includes (logged via console.warn so we\n       can tighten the schema once we know what tenants actually\n       ship in production).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"552681406e13e3cbcbde7fff963007f1fd1aed9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/552681406e13e3cbcbde7fff963007f1fd1aed9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDAyOGQ3Yzk1ODE4NjI0N2MxMmE3NTkxNGQ5NDk0MTg1YjQ3OTg4OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06","sha":"945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06"}],"sha":"028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/028d7c958186247c12a75914d9494185b479888c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:39:41Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:39:41Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(pgr): track auto-filled levels separately from manual selections\n\nPreviously the boundary cascade disabled any level that had a value\nwhen readOnly was true — including levels the user had just picked\nmanually. So if the map auto-fill missed (say) County, the user''s\nown click on the County dropdown would lock it disabled the moment\nthey made a selection.\n\nNow BoundaryComponent tracks `autoFilledKeys` — populated only by\nthe map-driven auto-fill effect, cleared whenever the user calls\nhandleSelection at that level (and on its descendants, which the\ncascade already resets). The disabled flag now reads\n`readOnly && autoFilledKeys[key] && selectedAtLevel`, so:\n\n- Map gave a clean path → all three levels read-only, just shown\n- Map missed at, say, the Ward level → County / Sub-County stay\n  read-only (auto-filled), Ward is interactive for manual pick\n- User changes a higher level after auto-fill → that level + all\n  child levels flip back to interactive\n\nAlso adds a temp debug log in the auto-fill effect that prints the\nhint, the boundary tree''s root types, and the resolved path. We''ve\nseen reports of County not pre-filling on naipepea even when the\nauto-fill is supposed to set it; the log will show whether\nfindWardPath is returning a path that includes the County node or\nstopping short. Will be removed once the root cause is confirmed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d294d0f5b0c612daec1aea38a561acfc8ff81258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/d294d0f5b0c612daec1aea38a561acfc8ff81258"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDk0NWE2ZDRkNjA5MjE1ZjlmMDhmOTNjYjQ0OWNiOTMzYWU5NzZlMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f","sha":"eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f"}],"sha":"945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/945a6d4d609215f9f08f93cb449cb933ae976e06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:36:44Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:36:44Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): readable disabled selects + lighter input placeholders\n\n- Override the v2 disabled-state `opacity: 50%` for boundary\n  dropdowns + pincode input on the citizen file-complaint location\n  step. The default reduction made auto-filled County / Sub-County /\n  Ward read as if they were empty (the user reported \"couldn''t see\n  county prefilled\"). Disabled fields now keep full opacity with a\n  faint off-white surface and `not-allowed` cursor as the read-only\n  cue, so the resolved value stays legible.\n\n- Lighten v2 input + textarea placeholder text to 35% black across\n  the citizen scope. Tailwind''s `placeholder:text-muted-foreground`\n  was rendering closer to body color on naipepea, making the\n  Landmark hint look like already-typed input. The new tone reads\n  clearly as ghost text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"59398c9e629a71bc771c9e7b895c087dc883423e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/59398c9e629a71bc771c9e7b895c087dc883423e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGViOTYyM2FiNDEwZmIxNDE5NTI3ZjZjNzk1ZWMzODNlMjhjMWExN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050","sha":"4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050"}],"sha":"eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/eb9623ab410fb1419527f6c795ec383e28c1a17f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:30:20Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:30:20Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"feat(pgr): collapse address+ward into single confirm-location step\n\nCitizen file-complaint flow drops from 6 steps to 5. The previous\nflow asked the user to re-pick County / Sub-County / Ward and re-type\nthe pincode — even though the prior map-pin step had already\ncaptured them via `GeoLocations.resolveWard()` (point-in-polygon on\nthe bundled Nairobi-wards GeoJSON) and Nominatim reverse-geocode.\n\nNew combined step:\n- Boundary cascade (PGRBoundaryComponent) auto-fills from the map\n  ward hint and renders each level as a DISABLED v2 Select with the\n  resolved value visible — read-only, can''t be changed.\n- Pincode field is disabled when the map''s Nominatim response gave\n  one. If Nominatim returned nothing, it stays editable.\n- Landmark text input is always editable (only field the user types).\n- If the boundary auto-fill misses a particular level (GeoJSON /\n  boundary-tree drift), that specific level becomes interactive so\n  the user can fill the gap manually — graceful degradation.\n\nMap step now requires `GeoLocationsPoint` (lat/lng) before Next,\nbacked by the existing default-pin seed on first load. There is no\n\"skip\" path on the citizen flow.\n\nPlumbing:\n- `BoundaryComponent` + `BoundaryDropdown` gained a `readOnly` prop\n  that disables a level only when both the caller asked for it AND\n  the level has a value (so empty levels stay interactive).\n- `STEPS`, `MANDATORY_BY_STEP`, `Step3Description`, `Step4Images`,\n  and the orchestrator''s index-based render switch all renumbered\n  to match the 5-step shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dbcf7188e8d51c28acd6ec1654df2b1b66bf77de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/dbcf7188e8d51c28acd6ec1654df2b1b66bf77de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDQwMTdiOTE5YzU3M2ZmZmI5MWE4YzQ2ODI1OTQwNDA1N2M3NzYwNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d","sha":"b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d"}],"sha":"4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/4017b919c573fffb91a8c468259404057c776050"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:21:08Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:21:08Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): citizen footer centred over content column, not viewport\n\nMirror the `.citizen-home-container` 260px gutter on the\n`.citizen-home-footer` when the v2 sidebar is mounted, so the\n\"Powered by DIGIT\" text lands at the centre of the right-side\ncontent column (the same column the form / module list occupies)\nrather than at the centre of the full viewport — where the text\npreviously sat visually aligned with the sidebar''s right edge.\n\nMobile: gutter resets to 0 so the footer text re-centres to the\nfull viewport (the v2 sidebar isn''t rendered there).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3903bdf0d2c649e8b699e050249b6081c09a78d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/f3903bdf0d2c649e8b699e050249b6081c09a78d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGI5MmRlOWNhYzQ4MzliMzUxNDA0MTA4NTA0ZmVkOTIzZDU5Y2Q3MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b","sha":"efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b"}],"sha":"b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/b92de9cac4839b351404108504fed923d59cd70d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:20:10Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:20:10Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): file-complaint full-width + dropdown popouts not clipped\n\n- `.pgr-citizen-wrapper` now `flex: 1 1 auto` so it fills the\n  available content width inside .citizen-home-container (was\n  shrinking to ~991px because it had no flex-grow and the now-fixed\n  v2 sidebar left only one flex child in the row). Wrapper takes\n  the full 1210px on a 1470px viewport.\n\n- Removed `overflowY: auto` (and the `minHeight: 0` that paired with\n  it) from the step body inside CreatePGRFlowV2. That was the\n  body-only-scroll pattern that clipped a Type/Subtype/Boundary\n  dropdown listbox when it tried to extend past the bottom of a\n  short form — testers got an internal scrollbar instead of the\n  dropdown floating over the underlying surface. With the wrapper\n  + scope + card all set to `overflow: visible`, the listbox spills\n  out cleanly. Form keeps its natural content height; long forms\n  scroll the page (global scroll), short forms stay short and\n  popovers fall outside the form boundary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"abad6e270972f0c2476d7d18326b77d23f0e8768","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/abad6e270972f0c2476d7d18326b77d23f0e8768"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGVmZDQ1ZTZjZDRlNjA2ZTM2ODE2NWQ0NTZkMjA3YTcxMWNlODRkMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f","sha":"dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f"}],"sha":"efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/efd45e6cd4e606e368165d456d207a711ce84d0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:15:56Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:15:56Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): citizen profile uses configurator tokens, not invented vars\n\nReverted the `--v2-sidebar-fg-strong` / `--color-sidebar-fg-strong`\nchain I added — those vars don''t exist in configurator''s color-config\nschema, so a tenant could never set them. The previous patch only\nworked because of the hardcoded fallback.\n\nNow wired through configurator-canonical tokens:\n- Avatar disc bg keeps a static rgba(255,255,255,0.92) — that''s a\n  design constant (like the 6px border radius), not a brand colour,\n  so it doesn''t need a theme variable.\n- Avatar initial reads `--color-sidebar-bg` so the monogram is the\n  same colour as the sidebar surface — the chip looks like a\n  cutout regardless of tenant palette.\n- Name + mobile + email all use `--color-sidebar-text-default`, which\n  the configurator color-config form already exposes. Hierarchy is\n  driven by font-weight (600 for name, 400 for contact lines) rather\n  than by an invented \"strong text\" token.\n\nIf a tenant ships a palette where light-gray text doesn''t read on\ntheir sidebar, they fix it where they always have — by overriding\n`--color-sidebar-text-default` in MDMS.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c685762f105df77464e03abef7771c9c1295741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/4c685762f105df77464e03abef7771c9c1295741"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGRiYWQ5MmQwODVjYTZmY2U2ZDk1NTI1MzQ4MDIyOTViYjczOTg0NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6","sha":"46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6"}],"sha":"dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/dbad92d085ca6fce6d9552534802295bb739846f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:13:18Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:13:18Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): citizen profile avatar + name readable on green sidebar\n\nThe Profile section in the v2 citizen sidebar was reading from\n`--color-sidebar-selected-text` for both the avatar bg/initial\ncontrast and the user''s name. That token is correctly meant as\n\"text on a yellow active row\" — naipepea sets it to dark green\n(#204F37) which works great on the yellow active item bg, but the\navatar + name sit directly on the green sidebar surface, where\nthe same dark green is invisible.\n\nAvatar now uses a white-ish (92% opacity) background with dark\ngreen initial — the disc reads as a distinct chip on the green\nsidebar with a legible monogram. Name flips to plain white so it\nstands out at the top of the sidebar regardless of how a tenant\nconfigures `--color-sidebar-selected-text`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9dcc878ae6a188c8bf5c204c7e623625ec80cc91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/9dcc878ae6a188c8bf5c204c7e623625ec80cc91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDQ2NTcwYjhjMjRjNjUwNjUxMDRkZmQ1ZDZiMjlhODI4ZjI5NjRhYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de","sha":"7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de"}],"sha":"46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/46570b8c24c65065104dfd5d6b29a828f2964ab6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:11:01Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:11:01Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): citizen login centered (sidebar-padding only when sidebar mounts)\n\nThe previous patch added `padding-left: 260px` to every\n`.citizen-home-container` so the main content cleared the now-fixed\nv2 sidebar. But the citizen login / OTP flow doesn''t mount the\nsidebar (logged-out), so the 260px gutter just shifted the centered\nlogin card 130px to the right of viewport center.\n\nScoped the rule via `:has(> aside.v2-scope)` so the padding only\nkicks in when the sidebar is actually rendered. Login card is\nviewport-centered again; all-services / file-complaint /\ncomplaint-details / edit-profile keep the sidebar reservation as\nbefore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d6731a5cc86a56131aaca87d7f736ab2be844ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/1d6731a5cc86a56131aaca87d7f736ab2be844ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDdjNjlmMWJiNWY5M2I5ODQ3OTlhZjBjYzQ4Mzc3ZDkxOTY0MWU2ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71","sha":"56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71"}],"sha":"7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/7c69f1bb5f93b984799af0cc48377d919641e6de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:09:22Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:09:22Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): citizen navbar revert + .digit-select chrome\n\nTwo follow-ups on PR #100 testers flagged after the input-consistency\npatch:\n\n- Citizen flow uses `.navbar` for the topbar, not `.digit-topbar`.\n  My earlier topbar-revert block only matched `.digit-topbar`, so\n  the citizen language dropdown was still picking up the unified\n  form-control chrome (white box / 6px / 44px on the green topbar).\n  Added `.navbar` (and `header.digit-header` for symmetry) to the\n  revert selector list — citizen + employee topbars now both fall\n  back to vendor defaults.\n\n- `.digit-select` (the date-range filter on /employee/pgr/inbox-v2,\n  among others) was missing from the unified rule''s selector list,\n  so it kept its dark vendor border + 4px radius — what the tester\n  called the \"boxy black border\" the page hadn''t shrugged off.\n  Added to the unified border / height / hover / focus selectors so\n  it converges on light-gray 1px / 6px / 44px like every other\n  input-like control.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7511d62ced4cd56e552d71214fa30866d09770a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/7511d62ced4cd56e552d71214fa30866d09770a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDU2ODg5YWIwY2Y0Y2QzNjBkOTBhYWE3YTQ3ZWNlYzg2M2QwNDBmNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424","sha":"2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424"}],"sha":"56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/56889ab0cf4cd360d90aaa7a47ecec863d040f71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:07:21Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T11:07:21Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): single-border inputs + footer next to citizen sidebar\n\n- Strip own chrome from inputs nested inside `.digit-text-input-field`.\n  The wrapper carries the visible 1px / 6px-radius border from the\n  unified rule; the unified rule was ALSO stamping the same chrome\n  on the inner `<input>` so the Complaint No / Mobile No filters\n  rendered with two visible borders (testers screenshot, follow-up\n  to PR #99). Override matches the unified rule''s `:not(...)` chain\n  to win the specificity tie. The prefix BUTTON keeps its yellow\n  tint + 1px right separator, but the wrapper itself is now plain\n  white instead of yellow — removes the triple-border on Mobile No.\n\n- Citizen v2 sidebar switched to `position: fixed` (top:56, left:0)\n  so it lifts out of the `.citizen-home-container` flex row. With\n  the sidebar out of the row''s intrinsic height, the row collapses\n  to its main-content height and the page footer (\"Powered by\n  DIGIT\") flows below the row at body bottom — visible in viewport\n  on short pages, alongside the sidebar, just like employee. Added\n  `padding-left: 260px` on the desktop `.citizen-home-container` so\n  main content doesn''t underlap the fixed sidebar; the rule\n  short-circuits on mobile (≤47.99rem) where the sidebar is hidden.\n\n- Loading-skeleton aside in citizen-sidebar.tsx synced to the same\n  fixed-position chrome so the skeleton state matches the loaded\n  state pixel-for-pixel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44c23cd951bf9489ce01b14d2252680dfe6972d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/44c23cd951bf9489ce01b14d2252680dfe6972d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDJmNWYwNDMzNmQzMmJmMThmOWFjMDcxZmM4YjNhNjQ5ZDAwNTY0MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f","sha":"5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f"}],"sha":"2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/2f5f04336d32bf18f9ac071fc8b3a649d0056424"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T10:58:58Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T10:58:58Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): unify input chrome + revert topbar + sidebar full-height\n\nFollow-up patches on the same branch (PR #100):\n\n- Unified input / dropdown / textarea border chrome across every\n  surface: 1px solid `var(--color-border)` (light gray), 6px radius,\n  44px height (textarea = auto, min 88px), surface bg, no shadows;\n  hover/focus → brand border. Replaces the patchwork of vendor\n  digit-* defaults and Tailwind border-input HSLs that produced\n  the boxy-black borders the testers flagged. OTP boxes\n  (`.v2-otp-box`), the citizen login phone input\n  (`.v2-login-phone-input`), the legacy employee sandbox OTP\n  (`.sandbox-otp-input`), and the inner display elements inside\n  dropdowns are excluded from the unified rule via :not() so they\n  keep their purpose-built chrome.\n\n- Topbar (citizen + employee) opts out of the unified rule entirely\n  via a `revert !important` reset block — the unified white-44px-\n  rounded look was painting \"white blocks\" on top of the green\n  topbar, which the user called out. Topbar dropdowns now keep\n  their pre-PR-100 vendor styling.\n\n- Citizen sidebar now extends from below the topbar all the way to\n  the viewport bottom (height: 100vh - topbar), matching the\n  employee sidebar behaviour. The page footer (\"Powered by DIGIT\")\n  flows in the body content column to the right of the sidebar\n  instead of forming a band underneath it. Required updating\n  `--v2-topbar-height` from a stale 82px (legacy topbar height) to\n  56px (actual height set in PR #99) so every consumer of that var\n  computes correctly.\n\n- Hover treatment on the citizen sidebar: hover bg keeps the\n  tenant''s `--color-sidebar-hover-bg` (light yellow on naipepea),\n  but text + icon flip to the dark sidebar bg colour\n  (`--color-sidebar-hover-text` → fallback to `--color-sidebar-bg`)\n  so labels stay readable on the pale hover surface. Removes the\n  light-gray-on-light-yellow contrast bug the user spotted.\n\n- Source-side: added `className=\"v2-otp-box\"` to citizen OTP boxes\n  and `className=\"v2-login-phone-input\"` to the citizen login\n  phone input so the unified rule''s :not() exclusions land cleanly.\n\nFiles:\n- packages/digit-ui-components-v2/src/components/layout/citizen-sidebar.tsx\n- packages/modules/core/src/pages/citizen/Login/SelectMobileNumber.js\n- packages/modules/core/src/pages/citizen/Login/SelectOtp.js\n- public/vendor/overrides.css\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f13ad259c1af36084b2ad91758d8a06121f490e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/f13ad259c1af36084b2ad91758d8a06121f490e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDU1NDg3NDE2ODVjZWU4MWEyZGQ0OTE1YWFjYzg1MTg0ZDZhOTBlNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/16c8bf0e2ee48215c99c221eaef30da077323a43","sha":"16c8bf0e2ee48215c99c221eaef30da077323a43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/16c8bf0e2ee48215c99c221eaef30da077323a43"}],"sha":"5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/5548741685cee81a2dd4915aacc85184d6a90e4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/16c8bf0e2ee48215c99c221eaef30da077323a43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T10:46:31Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T10:46:31Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(modernize): #538 alignment + restore global scroll\n\nAddresses egov/CCRS#538 + verbal feedback from Naipepea review of PR #99.\n\n- Sidebars (citizen + employee) re-tinted to themed green via\n  `--color-sidebar-bg` (Nairobi theme) with light foreground tokens.\n  The earlier white sidebars came from `--v2-surface-color` overrides;\n  switched both to the legacy `--color-sidebar-*` token chain so a\n  tenant''s MDMS theme drives every shade. Hover keeps the tenant''s\n  yellow tint (`--color-sidebar-hover-bg`) but flips text + icon to\n  dark green via `--color-sidebar-hover-text` so labels stay readable\n  on the pale hover surface (was blending with the light-gray\n  inactive text).\n\n- Global page scroll restored. Reverted the `.pgr-citizen-wrapper` +\n  `.v2-employee-create-complaint` flex-column-with-fixed-height\n  layout, the `ScreenContainer flex:1; min-h:0` rules, and the form\n  card `overflow-y:auto`. Forms now flow at content height; the page\n  (not the form) scrolls when content runs long. Matches the legacy\n  scroll behaviour testers expected.\n\n- Duplicate \"Create Complaint\" page header dropped — the FormComposerV2\n  card already carries its own header, the v2-employee-page-header\n  on top of it stole vertical space and compressed the form on\n  1280x720 displays (#538 bug 2).\n\n- Take Action bar on /employee/pgr/complaint-details now aligns with\n  the page content column. The bar stays fixed to viewport bottom\n  (clear of the 40px page footer band) but its `left` is clamped to\n  56px so it clears the sidebar at every hover state instead of\n  spilling under it. Height auto-sizes to the single Submit row.\n\nFiles:\n- packages/digit-ui-components-v2/src/components/layout/citizen-sidebar.tsx\n- packages/digit-ui-components-v2/src/components/layout/screen.tsx\n- products/pgr/src/pages/employee/CreateComplaint/index.js\n- public/vendor/overrides.css\n- public/vendor/tailwind.css (build artifact regen)\n\nCloses egovernments/Citizen-Complaint-Resolution-System#538\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c7a676d3e641da212ce540a5ddfa83998516f58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/6c7a676d3e641da212ce540a5ddfa83998516f58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/16c8bf0e2ee48215c99c221eaef30da077323a43","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"h