eived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/f86667757170f5393950d91964f77c37886ebc58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:33:25Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:33:25Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"chore(modernize): sticky form footer + sidebar minus page-footer height\n\n- FormFooter is now position: sticky; bottom: 0 with a solid surface +\n  top border. Long forms scroll behind it; the Cancel/Continue row stays\n  pinned to the bottom of the viewport. When the user reaches the page\n  end, sticky releases and the row sits naturally above the\n  citizen-home-footer (\"Powered by DIGIT\").\n\n- Cap .SideBarStatic to calc(100vh - topbar - page-footer) — both\n  values exposed as :root tokens so the math has one source of truth.\n  Page no longer requires a global scroll just to reveal the footer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"467b97d68145509286989eb17ff64f67376b978d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/467b97d68145509286989eb17ff64f67376b978d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/f86667757170f5393950d91964f77c37886ebc58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/f86667757170f5393950d91964f77c37886ebc58","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKGY4NjY2Nzc1NzE3MGY1MzkzOTUwZDkxOTY0Zjc3YzM3ODg2ZWJjNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938","sha":"34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938"}],"sha":"f86667757170f5393950d91964f77c37886ebc58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/f86667757170f5393950d91964f77c37886ebc58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:31:25Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:31:25Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"chore(modernize): theme-aware vars + sidebar height + dropdown left padding\n\nSidebar:\n- Cap .SideBarStatic to calc(100vh - 56px) so the page footer is visible\n  without scrolling on regular content pages.\n- 260px wide; 2-line clamp + word-break so long entries like \"Citizen\n  Complaint Resolution\" never hard-truncate.\n- Compact rhythm: 6/12 padding, 36px min row height, 1px gap.\n- Hover bg uses --color-grey-light (theme-neutral). Active uses\n  --color-primary-selected-bg + brand stripe via --color-primary-1\n  (falls back through --color-primary-main). Removes the previous yellow\n  active tint that fought the kenya-green theme.\n\nFooter:\n- Border + text colors use --color-border / --color-text-secondary /\n  --color-page-bg (all already defined in vendor digit-ui-css). No more\n  hardcoded greys.\n\nv2 components — replace hardcoded colors with theme-aware vars:\n- Card surface: var(--v2-surface-color, var(--color-surface, #ffffff))\n- Select listbox surface: same as Card\n- Label asterisk: var(--color-error, #d4351c)\nEach still falls back to a sensible default if the tenant doesn''t set\nthe var, so day-one rendering works without an MDMS update.\n\nSelect dropdown UX:\n- Move the tick to the left edge of the row, absolutely positioned at\n  0.5rem so non-selected rows show the same left padding (1.25rem) as\n  the label start. No more empty fixed-width slot eating space.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67ab4d13a47673f8ad3cd4a7ce82bd8420f4975a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/67ab4d13a47673f8ad3cd4a7ce82bd8420f4975a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDM0YmQwMjkwYTE0MDliM2YzOWI2ZjI5YmM3NDhkOWY2ZGYxMmM5Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105","sha":"16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105"}],"sha":"34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/34bd0290a1409b3f39b6f29bc748d9f6df12c938"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:25:05Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:25:05Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"chore(modernize): pull citizen file-complaint UX back toward legacy + sidebar/footer polish\n\nIterations on PR feedback (2026-05-06):\n\n- Drop the stepper entirely (was over-explaining a 6-step form)\n- Drop ScreenContainer''s narrow-centered column — form fills available\n  width, left-aligns with the parent BackButton again\n- Replace the sticky FormFooter (with backdrop-blur) with an inline border-\n  top action row inside the card — solid fills, no glassmorphism\n- Restore Select dropdown for complaint type + sub-type; the radio cards\n  felt too \"novel\" vs the legacy\n- Replace native <select> with a hand-rolled listbox component\n  (keyboard nav, type-ahead, click-outside) so we can style it to match v2\n  chrome and put the check on the left of each option\n- Inline safety nets for theme tokens that depend on a Tailwind recompile:\n  Card/listbox white background, required-label red asterisk, listbox\n  width:100% / max-height:16rem / z-index:9999 (vendor NEXT button can\n  overlay otherwise)\n\nSidebar (StaticCitizenSideBar) modernization in overrides.css:\n- 240px wide (was 219px) — long labels like \"Citizen Complaint\n  Resolution\" no longer truncate to \"Citizen Complaint R…\"\n- Allow up to 2-line wrap with -webkit-line-clamp:2; no clipping\n- Rounded 8px row surface, faint hover tint, branded left-edge accent\n  stripe + filled bg on the active row\n- Drop the dated underline-on-hover treatment\n\nCitizen footer modernization in overrides.css:\n- Soft top divider, balanced 14/16 padding, tasteful \"Powered by …\" sizing\n\nPlus: fix Tailwind --watch co-process exiting on startup (stdin was\n`ignore`; switched to `pipe` so tailwindcss keeps the watcher alive).\n\nPass `t` and a minimal `config` object through to GeoLocations,\nPGRBoundaryComponent, and SelectImages — they read `t` directly and crash\nwithout it. Wire StepShell description to a `tr()` helper that falls back\nto readable English when an MDMS key isn''t registered yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d35d5e57ba52d6668854894cbcbc38d50a759deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/d35d5e57ba52d6668854894cbcbc38d50a759deb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105","node_id":"C_kwDOSD-TUNoAKDE2YTk4OTY5MjJjYmEzNDM4NWMwNTgyNjE1ODIyMDM1Y2Y5NWQxMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commit/e6ba4ae0e579932a3ad62bdf5daaa1a1c0de89ec","sha":"e6ba4ae0e579932a3ad62bdf5daaa1a1c0de89ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e6ba4ae0e579932a3ad62bdf5daaa1a1c0de89ec"}],"sha":"16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/16a9896922cba34385c0582615822035cf95d105"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/e6ba4ae0e579932a3ad62bdf5daaa1a1c0de89ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T19:56:34Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T19:56:34Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"feat(modernize): foundation (Tailwind + shadcn-style v2) + citizen file-complaint migrated\n\nAuthorized by Chakshu (2026-05-05) to \"make the components on the egov app\nmodern\". This is the first PR in the digit-ui-esbuild ↔ digit-configurator\nstack convergence. Strangler-fig: legacy CSS + components stay as-is, v2\nships alongside them, only consumers we explicitly migrate use v2.\n\nFoundation\n- New package `packages/digit-ui-components-v2/` (TypeScript, scoped to a\n  `.v2-scope` selector so utility classes never bleed onto legacy pages).\n- Tailwind 3 wired into the existing esbuild pipeline as a co-process\n  (initial sync compile + `--watch`); production build calls `tailwindcss\n  --minify` once before esbuild. `node esbuild.dev.js` remains the single\n  dev entry — naipepea tmux command is unchanged.\n- Theme bridge: Tailwind tokens read from `--v2-*` HSL channel triples\n  that fall back to existing MDMS brand vars (`--color-text-primary`,\n  `--color-sidebar-bg`, …). kenya-green stays kenya-green automatically.\n- esbuild now resolves `.tsx`/`.ts` and the new `@egovernments/digit-ui-\n  components-v2` alias.\n- Primitives: Button (cva variants), Card+sub-parts, Input, Textarea,\n  Label, Field, RadioCards, Select, FileUpload.\n- Layout: ScreenContainer, ScreenHeader, FormFooter (sticky action bar,\n  safe-area aware), BackLink, Stepper.\n- Form chrome: `useMultiStepForm` hook.\n\nFirst migration — citizen file-complaint\n- `products/pgr/src/pages/citizen/Create/CreatePGRFlowV2.tsx` replaces the\n  FormExplorer + FormComposerV2 + steps-config/* stack. Module.js''s\n  `CreatePGRFlow` registration now points at v2.\n- Same 6-step shape preserved (type → map → address → ward → details →\n  photos) so the data sent to `/pgr/v1/_create` is byte-identical and the\n  Redux + response page see no change.\n- Step-1 type/sub-type now uses RadioCards + native Select — far better\n  mobile tap targets vs the old micro-dropdown.\n- Reuses GeoLocations, PGRBoundaryComponent, SelectImages as embedded\n  sub-components (skin first, gut later).\n- Sticky FormFooter with Back / Continue|Submit, mobile-first layout, real\n  stepper, native validation messages.\n- Pincode allowlist + ward-leaf checks ported verbatim from FormExplorer\n  (CCRS#469 + #478 stay closed).\n\nOut of scope (this PR)\n- Other surfaces — only `/citizen/pgr/create-complaint` touches v2.\n- Dead code: `pages/citizen/Create/CitizenCreate.js` and the unused\n  `Steps/`/`steps-config/` files. FormExplorer.js stays in the tree as a\n  one-release rollback path; can be deleted after naipepea verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7f6ad32dfcf56da6387acca48dfa69a358f9ad69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/7f6ad32dfcf56da6387acca48dfa69a358f9ad69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/e6ba4ae0e579932a3ad62bdf5daaa1a1c0de89ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsig