or":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prtkjakhar","id":65057795,"login":"prtkjakhar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDU3Nzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prtkjakhar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/commits/11799a2bd7f2225238dfdbfe7625132fb4ab8bde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T11:07:27Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T11:07:27Z","email":"prtkjakhar@gmail.com","name":"Prateek Jakhar"},"message":"fix(auth): close citizen↔employee cross-surface hole + URL-aware redirect\n\nPrivateRoute had two problems behind the user-reported \"citizen logged-\nin users can access employee flows / vice versa\" and \"token expiry\ndoesn''t take you to the right login\":\n\n1. **Login-redirect target was derived from `Storage.get(\"userType\")`,\n   not from the URL the user was trying to reach.** `userType` is set\n   when a /citizen or /employee App component last mounted — so a\n   citizen token + a navigate to /employee/... still resolved\n   `userType === \"citizen\"` and bounced the user to `/citizen/login`\n   when their token expired, even though they''d been on the employee\n   surface. Derive the target from the path itself\n   (`/<contextPath>/employee/...` → employee, anything else → citizen)\n   so an expired session always lands on the right login.\n\n2. **Any non-empty access_token was treated as \"logged in\" regardless\n   of token type.** A citizen-typed token therefore passed PrivateRoute\n   for `/employee/...` and rendered the employee component (which\n   would then 401 from the API or show partial UI). Add a\n   `tokenUserType !== expectedFromUrl` check that redirects mismatched\n   sessions back to the surface''s own login.\n\nBoth copies of PrivateRoute (react-components and digit-ui-components)\nget the same treatment. Verified on local desktop:\n\n- Citizen-token user visiting `/employee/pgr/inbox-v2` is redirected\n  to `/employee/user/language-selection` (was: rendering the inbox).\n- Cleared storage + visiting `/citizen/...` flows through the new\n  no-token path.\n- Cleared storage + visiting `/employee/...` redirects to the employee\n  login.\n\nNote: citizen routes like `/citizen/all-services` are wrapped in plain\n`<Route>` not `<PrivateRoute>` so this fix doesn''t gate them. Wrapping\nthose is a separate refactor; flagged for a follow-up. The Axios\n`InvalidAccessTokenException` interceptor (Request.js) already routes\n401s to the right login based on URL, so token-expiry mid-session is\ncovered as long as the path matches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e132f366a3fef6bab661aad01db9d80a86d823be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/trees/e132f366a3fef6bab661aad01db9d80a86d823be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theflywheel/digit-ui-esbuild/git/commits/11799a2bd7f2225238dfdbfe7625132fb4ab8bde","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65057795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.