oredDate":"2026-03-09T07:43:38Z","committedDate":"2026-03-09T07:43:38Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Enkhtuvshin0513","providerType":"User"},"email":"37796969+Enkhtuvshin0513@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Enkhtuvshin Narmandakh"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:40:50.376Z","repositoryId":1212707245,"sha":"6ff44a4e8983bacf6a15056c5aa59d19c52f05ba"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:40:50.376Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104069564?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Wlkr123","id":104069564,"login":"Wlkr123","node_id":"U_kgDOBjP5vA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/local-dev-appsec-org/erxes/commits/ebed2f81fc5e1fdc18442861be24b3d415aff37d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T12:24:21Z","email":"104069564+Wlkr123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tuguldur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T12:24:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fixes core (#7213)\n\n* feat: migrate automations trigger to tRPC transport\n\nAdds tRPC support for automation triggers with fallback to BullMQ. Implements tRPC endpoint in automations service, adds transport option to sendAutomationTrigger, and migrates Facebook automation to use tRPC transport.\n\n* fix: use replaceAll instead of replace in sanitizeFilename\n\nReplace single replace() calls with replaceAll() for illegalRe, controlRe, reservedRe, and windowsReservedRe patterns to ensure all occurrences are sanitized from filenames.\n\n* feat: implement activity logging for user actions\n\n- Introduced a new ActivityLogs model to handle user activity logging.\n- Updated connection resolvers to utilize the new activity logging methods.\n- Refactored existing user-related mutations to streamline activity log creation.\n- Added utility functions for building user activity logs based on changes in user fields, roles, and assignments.\n- Removed deprecated event dispatcher functionality to simplify the logging process.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 20a709d according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* feat(activity-logs): enhance activity log rendering and context handling\n\n- Added `getProductDisplayText` utility to improve product display in activity logs.\n- Refactored event handler context management to use `AsyncLocalStorage` for better context handling.\n- Introduced new `context` field in activity log payloads to include additional information.\n- Implemented custom activity log components for customer and team member activities.\n- Improved activity log sentence formatting for better readability and clarity.\n- Created utility functions for formatting activity values and extracting changed values.\n- Modularized actor-related functions for better maintainability and reusability.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in cd3d18c according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* feat(activity-logs): enhance activity log components and add custom activity handling\n\n- Introduced AssignmentSentence and DefaultActivityRow components for better activity representation.\n- Added PermissionGroupAssignmentSentence and PropertiesFieldChangeSentence components to handle specific activity types.\n- Implemented custom activity rendering for deals, including DealCreatedRow, DealMovedRow, and DealAssignmentRow.\n- Enhanced activity log context to support custom activities and limit fetching.\n- Refactored utility functions for better property field value formatting and handling.\n- Updated activity log types to accommodate new fields and ensure type safety.\n- Improved date formatting in activity logs for better readability.\n- Added hooks for managing property field changes and multi-select computations.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in f94fce0 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* feat(activity-logs): implement cursor-based pagination and variant handling for activity logs\n\n* feat: enhance activity log functionality and improve code structure\n\n- Added custom permissions handling in permission mutation resolver.\n- Updated product activity log resolvers to use ITag type for added and removed labels.\n- Refactored automation message sending to improve type safety and clarity.\n- Improved activity log builder by reorganizing imports and ensuring consistent formatting.\n- Simplified plugin start logic by removing unnecessary null checks.\n- Enhanced sales API activity log resolvers with ITag type for better type safety.\n- Fixed automation service main file to use a consistent Redis key for service address.\n- Updated TRPC automation trigger to include processId in context.\n- Added detailed developer walkthrough for activity log implementation in documentation.\n- Refactored company and product activity rows to use index as key for badges.\n- Cleaned up member activity rows by removing unused UserFieldChangedRow component.\n- Improved assignment sentence components by using index as key for badges.\n- Fixed rendering issues in default activity sentences by removing unnecessary semicolons.\n- Updated permission group assignment sentences to use index as key for badges.\n- Enhanced deal activity rows to ensure proper rendering of activity descriptions.\n- Refactored description changed activity row to accept activity as a prop for better clarity.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 992ec81 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* refactor: change export to type export for event types in index.ts\n\n* refactor: consolidate utility imports from ''erxes-api-shared/utils''\n\n* refactor: streamline activity log generation and enhance deal watch functionality\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in fc92c61 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* refactor: remove unused dependencies from content_api and frontline_api\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 5d178bd according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in d43ad3d according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: deepsource-autofix[bot] <62050782+deepsource-autofix[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4211fefbad7423c6ba3f565451451526602890bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/local-dev-appsec-org/erxes/git/trees/4211fefbad7423c6ba3f565451451526602890bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/local-dev-appsec-org/erxes/git/commits/ebed2f81fc5e1fdc18442861be24b3d415aff37d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4211fefbad7423c6ba3f565451451526602890bd\nparent 9776d3954dc42fdfe2478230b71f6c1a94a9e4a4\nauthor Tuguldur <104069564+Wlkr123@users.noreply.github.com> 1774355061 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774355061 +0800\n\nFixes core (#7213)\n\n* feat: migrate automations trigger to tRPC transport\n\nAdds tRPC support for automation triggers with fallback to BullMQ. Implements tRPC endpoint in automations service, adds transport option to sendAutomationTrigger, and migrates Facebook automation to use tRPC transport.\n\n* fix: use replaceAll instead of replace in sanitizeFilename\n\nReplace single replace() calls with replaceAll() for illegalRe, controlRe, reservedRe, and windowsReservedRe patterns to ensure all occurrences are sanitized from filenames.\n\n* feat: implement activity logging for user actions\n\n- Introduced a new ActivityLogs model to handle user activity logging.\n- Updated connection resolvers to utilize the new activity logging methods.\n- Refactored existing user-related mutations to streamline activity log creation.\n- Added utility functions for building user activity logs based on changes in user fields, roles, and assignments.\n- Removed deprecated event dispatcher functionality to simplify the logging process.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 20a709d according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* feat(activity-logs): enhance activity log rendering and context handling\n\n- Added `getProductDisplayText` utility to improve product display in activity logs.\n- Refactored event handler context management to use `AsyncLocalStorage` for better context handling.\n- Introduced new `context` field in activity log payloads to include additional information.\n- Implemented custom activity log components for customer and team member activities.\n- Improved activity log sentence formatting for better readability and clarity.\n- Created utility functions for formatting activity values and extracting changed values.\n- Modularized actor-related functions for better maintainability and reusability.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in cd3d18c according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* feat(activity-logs): enhance activity log components and add custom activity handling\n\n- Introduced AssignmentSentence and DefaultActivityRow components for better activity representation.\n- Added PermissionGroupAssignmentSentence and PropertiesFieldChangeSentence components to handle specific activity types.\n- Implemented custom activity rendering for deals, including DealCreatedRow, DealMovedRow, and DealAssignmentRow.\n- Enhanced activity log context to support custom activities and limit fetching.\n- Refactored utility functions for better property field value formatting and handling.\n- Updated activity log types to accommodate new fields and ensure type safety.\n- Improved date formatting in activity logs for better readability.\n- Added hooks for managing property field changes and multi-select computations.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in f94fce0 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* feat(activity-logs): implement cursor-based pagination and variant handling for activity logs\n\n* feat: enhance activity log functionality and improve code structure\n\n- Added custom permissions handling in permission mutation resolver.\n- Updated product activity log resolvers to use ITag type for added and removed labels.\n- Refactored automation message sending to improve type safety and clarity.\n- Improved activity log builder by reorganizing imports and ensuring consistent formatting.\n- Simplified plugin start logic by removing unnecessary null checks.\n- Enhanced sales API activity log resolvers with ITag type for better type safety.\n- Fixed automation service main file to use a consistent Redis key for service address.\n- Updated TRPC automation trigger to include processId in context.\n- Added detailed developer walkthrough for activity log implementation in documentation.\n- Refactored company and product activity rows to use index as key for badges.\n- Cleaned up member activity rows by removing unused UserFieldChangedRow component.\n- Improved assignment sentence components by using index as key for badges.\n- Fixed rendering issues in default activity sentences by removing unnecessary semicolons.\n- Updated permission group assignment sentences to use index as key for badges.\n- Enhanced deal activity rows to ensure proper rendering of activity descriptions.\n- Refactored description changed activity row to accept activity as a prop for better clarity.\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 992ec81 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* refactor: change export to type export for event types in index.ts\n\n* refactor: consolidate utility imports from ''erxes-api-shared/utils''\n\n* refactor: streamline activity log generation and enhance deal watch functionality\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in fc92c61 according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* refactor: remove unused dependencies from content_api and frontline_api\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in 5d178bd according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n* Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability\n\n* style: format code with Prettier\n\nThis commit fixes the style issues introduced in d43ad3d according to the output\nfrom Prettier.\n\nDetails: https://github.com/erxes/erxes/pull/7213\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: deepsource-autof