om/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/cfcaf61f069e0dc6d3c0dc2c9b5a63c31965f9b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:47:43Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:47:43Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Tag fields render as colored pills, not raw JSON\n\nThe Contact / Product / CustomizationManifest / SagaTemplate forms\nwere rendering the `tags` field as a raw JSON textarea showing\n{\"key\":\"value\"} — confusing and unusable. The widget registry\nalready has a TagField that renders colored pills with autocomplete\nand an X to remove; we just had the wrong view-type. Switched all\nfour from type:''json'' to type:''tags'' so the pill UI kicks in.","tree":{"sha":"d67b8a47a7ab7094d14aee3a63fb0fcee7aedd9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/d67b8a47a7ab7094d14aee3a63fb0fcee7aedd9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/cfcaf61f069e0dc6d3c0dc2c9b5a63c31965f9b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/cfcaf61f069e0dc6d3c0dc2c9b5a63c31965f9b8","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKGNmY2FmNjFmMDY5ZTBkYzZkM2MwZGMyYzliNWE2M2MzMTk2NWY5Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a","sha":"702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a"}],"sha":"cfcaf61f069e0dc6d3c0dc2c9b5a63c31965f9b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/cfcaf61f069e0dc6d3c0dc2c9b5a63c31965f9b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:44:58Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:44:58Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Pre-populate create-mode forms from model defaults\n\nThe new-Contact form opened with Type empty and Active off even\nthough the Contact model declares kind.default=''individual'' and\nisActive.default=true. Same bug applies to every model with\nschema-level defaults — they never reached the create form.\n\nTwo-step generic fix so this works for every model, no per-form\nwiring:\n\npackages/core/src/model/viewEnricher.ts\n  When merging model schema into a view definition, also copy each\n  field''s `default` value down to the view''s per-field def. Skip\n  SQL-function defaults (CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, gen_random_uuid(), …) —\n  those are server-side concerns and would only confuse the client.\n  View can still override by setting its own `default`.\n\nmodules/web/components/views/form/FormView.tsx\n  On mount in create mode (no recordId), walk the resolved\n  definition.fields and seed formData with any `default` values.\n  Runs once per definition; doesn''t clobber user edits.\n\nEffect across the app:\n  • Contact form: Type pre-selects \"Individual\", Active toggles on\n  • User form: Status pre-selects \"Active\" (matching today''s model\n    change in 313cb28)\n  • Company / Branch / Department / etc — all status enum defaults\n    flow through automatically\n  • Boolean toggles (isSellable, isPurchasable, isCustomer …) show\n    their declared default\n  • Every future model that declares `default:` benefits for free","tree":{"sha":"be6fa1fb2cca2976b573ec93673abaf7534149b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/be6fa1fb2cca2976b573ec93673abaf7534149b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDcwMjk4MDEwMWQxMWE0ZDMwMmQ4Mjk3Nzk3YzExNzAwMDNkYmQyMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29","sha":"3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29"}],"sha":"702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/702980101d11a4d302d8297797c1170003dbd21a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:37:46Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:37:46Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Polish the record-details sidebar + sane defaults\n\nFive fixes prompted by a screenshot of the form-view side panel\nshowing raw snake_case translation keys, a useless internal id row,\nand a generic \"Add attachment\" link with no hint about what types\nof files the system accepts.\n\nmodules/base/i18n/en_US.ts + ar_SA.ts\n  Add the entire base.sidebar.* namespace (record_details, info,\n  assignees, no_assignees, assign, tags, tag_name, add_tag,\n  attachments, add_attachment, upload_image, upload_document,\n  upload_any, drop_files, notes, add_note, save_note, no_notes,\n  activity, no_activity) plus base.field.created / modified /\n  created_by — these were referenced by the sidebar component but\n  never translated, so the t() helper was returning the trailing\n  key fragment (\"record_details\", \"no_assignees\", \"add_tag\" …)\n  instead of human text. Full English + Arabic.\n\nmodules/web/components/views/shared/FormSidebar.tsx\n  • INFO section: drop the raw record-id row. End users don''t need\n    to see \"452c034b-a71…\"; the dev panel surfaces it for\n    debugging. Removed the now-orphan Link2 import too.\n  • Notes section (new, between Tags and Attachments):\n    - Click-to-edit view of record.notes / .note / .description\n    - Textarea + Save / Cancel buttons; persists via PUT on the\n      record\n    - Empty-state shows \"+ Add a note…\"\n  • Attachments upload UI: replaced the lonely \"+ Add attachment\"\n    text link with a 3-column grid of labelled dashed-border\n    drop targets — Image / Document / Any file — each with its\n    own icon and an accept= filter that constrains the native\n    file picker. Now obvious what users can attach.\n  • Attachment list rows pick an icon by mime type\n    (ImageIcon for image/*, FileText for pdf/doc, FileIcon\n    otherwise) instead of always showing FileText.\n\nmodules/base/models/User.model.ts\n  status default ''pending'' → ''active''. New users could not log in\n  out of the box because they sat in a pending state nothing flips\n  to active automatically. Brings User in line with the existing\n  Company / Branch / Department defaults. Tenants that want a\n  manual approval flow override on create or via a workflow.","tree":{"sha":"78cc8c03768a24b45594063e44f030c0a8efdd74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/78cc8c03768a24b45594063e44f030c0a8efdd74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDNkNGZjYWVmYzg0YzAxN2NiZGZlYzk5ODMyM2UzNzljODNmNWJiMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8","sha":"8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8"}],"sha":"3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/3d4fcaefc84c017cbdfec998323e379c83f5bb29"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:25:38Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:25:38Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Make the default CompanyTheme platform-shareable\n\nSame fix as the marketing_templates change in e47c66f, same root\ncause: a starter record (base.theme_buildlish_default) requires a\ncompanyId that doesn''t exist at bootstrap, leaving every fresh\ninstall with one ugly \"null value in column companyid\" error in\nthe boot log and no default theme applied.\n\nmodules/base/models/CompanyTheme.model.ts\n  companyId — drop required:true. null now means \"platform-default\n  theme available to every company under the tenant\". Companies\n  override by creating their own record with companyId set.\n  Per-company active-theme uniqueness (deactivateOtherThemes)\n  already scopes by companyId, so a platform default and a\n  company override coexist cleanly.\n\nmodules/base/index.ts\n  Defensive ALTER TABLE company_themes ALTER COLUMN companyid\n  DROP NOT NULL in initialize() — drops the constraint on\n  previously-deployed databases. try/catch makes it safe to\n  re-run on every boot.\n\nVerified: zero \"null value in column companyid\" errors on restart.\nBoth Base and Marketing module data seeded successfully.","tree":{"sha":"768acf58098f7ef19540f828cf489c349874bb05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/768acf58098f7ef19540f828cf489c349874bb05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDhjODRiNTU4N2YyY2QxY2M2NGI3ZDYwNTcxNWIyZjU3Yjg1M2JkZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f","sha":"1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f"}],"sha":"8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/8c84b5587f2cd1cc64b7d605715b2f57b853bdd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:23:46Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:23:46Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Make marketing templates platform-shareable\n\nThe 5 seed templates (Welcome Email, Newsletter, Promotional Offer,\nAbandoned Cart, Re-engagement) failed to insert with NOT NULL\nviolation on companyid. Forcing a companyId on starter templates\ncreates a bootstrap chicken-and-egg: the seed runs before any\ncompany exists, and picking one arbitrarily privileges a single\ntenant.\n\nBetter semantic: companyId is now optional. `null` means\n\"platform-default template shared across every company under this\ntenant\"; setting it pins the template to one company. Companies\ncan clone-and-customize.\n\nmodules/marketing/models/MarketingTemplate.model.ts\n  companyId: drop required:true; add comment explaining the\n  null = platform-default convention.\n\nmodules/marketing/index.ts\n  Defensive ALTER TABLE in initialize() — drops the existing\n  NOT NULL constraint on already-deployed databases (createTable\n  IF NOT EXISTS skips column updates). try/catch so it''s safe to\n  rerun on every boot.\n\nVerified: dev server restart shows zero \"null value in column\ncompanyid of relation marketing_templates\" errors, and\n\"Marketing module data seeded\" logs cleanly.","tree":{"sha":"2c7bd6c4375fb60ddb8f083fc190d2b17ae24421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/2c7bd6c4375fb60ddb8f083fc190d2b17ae24421"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDExMDhjM2I2OWFkYjdlMjEwMDdhNDcwY2M0ZDczM2FlNTgwNjYyOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56","sha":"c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56"}],"sha":"1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/1108c3b69adb7e21007a470cc4d733ae5806628f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T15:53:00Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T15:53:00Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Fix view + seed validator warnings across products, marketing,\nmonitor, social\n\nmodules/products/views/index.ts\n  Default orderBy in the auto-view helper now picks a column that\n  actually exists on the model: prefer `name` if present, then\n  `sequence`, then `id`. The pricelist_item view in particular has\n  neither name nor sequence, so the old \"orderBy: [''name'']\" default\n  triggered \"orderBy field ''name'' not found in model schema\" — now\n  it orders by pricelistId + minQuantity desc.\n\nmodules/marketing/data/sequences.ts\nmodules/monitor/data/sequences.ts\nmodules/social/data/sequences.ts\n  Seed data was writing `padding` and `nextNumber` but the Sequence\n  model schema names those columns `paddingLength` and `currentValue`.\n  Renamed in the seed files. Also nudged the starting `currentValue`\n  to 0 (the first issued number then becomes 1 via increment).\n\nmodules/marketing/views/campaign.views.ts\n  Removed the orphan `campaignId` field from the campaign form view\n  — MarketingCampaign has no such column. Audience selection lives\n  on the marketing_campaign_audiences join table; left the Audience\n  tab in place with an empty group so it''s obvious where the\n  one2many relation should plug in later.","tree":{"sha":"7a1d9bab442f31b5c87a8c509791374c64a86e5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/7a1d9bab442f31b5c87a8c509791374c64a86e5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKGMxZGJmNWQ4YWY0YzQwYzkxYWRkY2M4Y2Q5M2QwNjc1Mjk4ZTFmNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812","sha":"e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812"}],"sha":"c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/c1dbf5d8af4c40c91addcc8cd93d0675298e1f56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T15:20:31Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T15:20:31Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Extract services/platform/ to its own repo\n\nThe Buildlish landing page + SaaS portal lives at\n~/buildlish-platform/ now, with a fresh git history, .gitignore,\n.env.example, and a README explaining how it connects to the\ngateway over HTTP via NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILDLISH_API_URL. It deploys\nindependently of the framework (Vercel-ready) so the framework\nrepo stays focused on the open-source product.\n\n  • Removed services/platform/ from this monorepo\n  • Removed the --filter=!@buildlish/platform exclusion from the\n    root dev script (no longer needed)\n  • Regenerated pnpm-lock.yaml — drops platform''s resolved deps\n\nNext: push the new repo to its own GitHub remote once a URL is\nprovided. Until then it lives locally at ~/buildlish-platform.","tree":{"sha":"9be341f42374dbb2ed74b6d7d60e31f6c7414cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/9be341f42374dbb2ed74b6d7d60e31f6c7414cb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKGU4ZDdkYjgxODRjZWIzZGZkODRkNzkzY2ZkNmExY2VhMzlhNTM4MTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed","sha":"bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed"}],"sha":"e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/e8d7db8184ceb3dfd84d793cfd6a1cea39a53812"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T14:19:59Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T14:19:59Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Fix module loader so newly-discovered modules actually load\n\nTwo bugs that together caused contacts, products, invoicing,\ncustomization, federation, marketing, monitor, social, and workflow\nto be discovered (21 manifests) but silently filtered out at boot\n(only 12 loaded). After this fix all 21 load and the auto-generated\nREST + MCP tools jump from 418 → 665 tools.\n\npackages/core/src/module/ModuleLoader.ts\n  syncModulesToDatabase() inserts a row into `modules` for every\n  newly-discovered manifest. The table is multi-tenant, so the row\n  needs tenant_id, but sync runs at boot before any request has set\n  TenantContext. Without an explicit tenant the INSERT failed with\n  NOT NULL violation 23502, the modules table never got the new\n  rows, and filterByDatabaseStatus then refused to load those\n  manifests on this and every subsequent boot.\n\n  Fix derives the platform tenant from real data — no hardcoded\n  UUIDs:\n    1. Reuse the tenant of any existing module row (the system was\n       originally installed under it; that tenant is the source of\n       truth for platform metadata).\n    2. Fall back to operator-supplied DEFAULT_TENANT_ID env var.\n    3. If neither is available, skip the sync and log a clear\n       warning so the operator knows to complete admin setup or\n       set the env var. No INSERT attempted with NULL.\n\n  Also fixes the column name — passes snake_case `tenant_id` since\n  BaseModel.create lowercases keys but doesn''t snake-case-convert\n  them, so `tenantId` would hit a \"column tenantid does not exist\"\n  error (42703).\n\n  New private resolvePlatformTenantId(ModuleModel) helper houses\n  the lookup logic.\n\nmodules/invoicing/models/Invoice.model.ts\n  Remove `default: ''CURRENT_DATE''` on issueDate — the DDL builder\n  quoted it as a string literal which Postgres rejected as an\n  invalid date format (22007 DateTimeParseError), preventing the\n  invoices table from being created. Date defaults are handled at\n  the application layer when posting the invoice.\n\nVerified:\n  • Boot log shows \"Module loading complete. 21 modules loaded\"\n  • MCP tools/list returns 665 tools (was 418); 65 new tools across\n    contacts, contact_categories, contact_tags, products,\n    product_categories, uoms, pricelists, pricelist_items, invoices,\n    invoice_lines, payments, saga_templates, customization_manifests\n  • REST /api/v1/{contacts,uoms,services} respond 401 (auth gate\n    works — auto-generated endpoints are live)","tree":{"sha":"ade6077df16f0144bd3c851f2d7d75965e82d372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/ade6077df16f0144bd3c851f2d7d75965e82d372"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKGJmMzVlOGZlYzI4NjZkY2E2MzAwNjgwOWFlODRmM2ZkMGRlZGU5ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632","sha":"742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632"}],"sha":"bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/bf35e8fec2866dca63006809ae84f3fd0dede9ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T16:03:06Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T16:03:06Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Universal Business Pack v1 — contacts + products + invoicing\n\nThree modules every business needs, regardless of industry. A retailer,\nagency, consultancy, restaurant, clinic, or freelancer can all run\ntheir core operations on this pack without writing code. Industry packs\n(automotive, healthcare, legal, etc.) are now layered extensions on top.\n\nmodules/contacts/ — universal contact management\n  Contact            polymorphic person/company; isCustomer / isVendor /\n                     isLead / isPartner flags (a contact can be many\n                     things at once); identity (name, code, salutation,\n                     job title, legal name, industry, employee count);\n                     org hierarchy via parentId; full comms (email,\n                     phone, mobile, fax, website, socialLinks jsonb);\n                     structured address (line1/line2/city/state/postal/\n                     countryId); commercial (taxId, paymentTerms,\n                     currency, creditLimit, discount %); classification\n                     (category + tags jsonb); soft fields (notes,\n                     avatar, color, metadata).\n  ContactCategory    hierarchical taxonomy with color + icon\n  ContactTag         flat lightweight labels\n  Seed: Customer / Vendor / Lead / Partner / Prospect categories.\n\nmodules/products/ — universal catalog\n  Product            6 types (good | service | subscription | digital |\n                     consumable | bundle); SKU + barcode + internal\n                     code; categoryId + brand + tags; uom + weight +\n                     volume; sales / purchase / cost prices in any\n                     currency; taxPercent; isSellable / isPurchasable /\n                     isStockTracked flags; primary image + jsonb\n                     gallery.\n  ProductCategory    hierarchical\n  Uom                multi-category (unit / weight / length / volume /\n                     time / area) with factor + rounding for safe\n                     conversions\n  Pricelist          named price scheme with currency + validity window\n  PricelistItem      match by product / category / min qty, rule of\n                     fixed | discount_pct | cost_plus_pct\n  Seeds: 12 standard UoMs (kg/g/ton/lb/m/cm/km/h/min/day/unit/dozen)\n         + 6 product categories.\n\nmodules/invoicing/ — universal billing\n  Invoice            4 types (customer_invoice / vendor_bill /\n                     customer_credit / vendor_refund); sequence-assigned\n                     number on post; reference / PO; issue/due/posted\n                     dates; currency; subtotal/tax/discount/total/paid/\n                     due totals; status (draft / posted / paid /\n                     partially_paid / cancelled / overdue); notes +\n                     internal note + metadata.\n  InvoiceLine        product-linked or free-text; quantity + uom + unit\n                     price + discount % + tax %; snapshot fields\n                     (name, sku) so a product rename never alters\n                     history; pre-computed subtotal / tax_amount /\n                     total per line.\n  Payment            inbound or outbound, optionally invoice-linked\n                     (one invoice → many payments for partial pay);\n                     6 methods (cash / bank_transfer / card / check /\n                     mobile_wallet / crypto / other); status (draft /\n                     pending / completed / failed / refunded).\n  Depends on contacts (contactId FK) + products (productId FK on lines).\n\nEach module follows the Buildlish conventions: manifest.json, full\nlifecycle index.ts (initialize → generateApis → seed), models/ with\nregister helper, views/ (list + form for every model with auto-laid\nforms), menus/ grouped per app, en + ar i18n.\n\n226/226 tests still pass. Zero new type errors. 43 files, 1762 lines.","tree":{"sha":"53a64d1d58bfd2a727e066779a2fe747956b3690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/53a64d1d58bfd2a727e066779a2fe747956b3690"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDc0MmViZmU0MTU2M2JjNWNmMGFkOTNhNGVjZDdiZmI5ZmU0MGM2MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea","sha":"2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea"}],"sha":"742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/742ebfe41563bc5cf0ad93a4ecd7bfb9fe40c632"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T15:23:08Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T15:23:08Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Phase 3e — gRPC transport (opt-in) alongside HTTP\n\nAdds gRPC as an alternative transport for cross-service calls — HTTP/2\nmultiplexing, smaller payloads, lower latency for high-frequency calls.\nOpt-in per service via the manifest. Functionally equivalent to HTTP:\nsame auth, same tenant propagation, same circuit breaker, same W3C\ntrace context propagation.\n\nDesign choice: one generic .proto with a single Invoke RPC carrying\nJSON payloads. No per-model code generation required, no extra build\nstep, and user-defined dynamic models work automatically. We still get\nHTTP/2''s framing/multiplexing benefits without forcing every module\nauthor to maintain typed protos.\n\nNew: packages/core/src/service/grpc/\n  • proto/gateway.proto      single Invoke(InvokeRequest) RPC with\n                             table + op + payload_json + context map +\n                             traceparent string\n  • loadProto.ts             runtime loader via @grpc/proto-loader\n  • GrpcServer.ts            createGrpcServer({ port, internalSecret })\n                             dispatches every Invoke to ModelRegistry\n                             with full TenantContext propagation\n                             (tenant/user/company/dept/branch/locale/\n                             permissions/groups), W3C trace extraction\n                             from metadata, span around every call,\n                             error → HTTP-equivalent status\n  • GrpcClient.ts            pooled HTTP/2 channels keyed by endpoint\n                             with keep-alive, 4 MB message limits\n  • GrpcRemoteService.ts     mirrors RemoteService surface (findById /\n                             findAll / create / update / delete /\n                             count / findOne / invoke) over gRPC.\n                             Circuit-breaker + adaptive deadline reuse\n                             the same instances as the HTTP path.\n\nManifest extension (ServiceRegistry.ts)\n  Adds grpcPort, grpcEndpoint, transport: ''http'' | ''grpc'' to\n  ServiceManifest. When transport === ''grpc'' on the target service,\n  RemoteService.json maps standard REST paths\n    GET    /api/v1/{table}/{id}        → findById\n    POST   /api/v1/{table}/search      → findAll\n    POST   /api/v1/{table}/count       → count\n    POST   /api/v1/{table}             → create\n    PUT    /api/v1/{table}/{id}        → update\n    DELETE /api/v1/{table}/{id}[?force]→ delete\n  into Invoke calls. Non-matching paths (attachments, custom routes)\n  fall through to HTTP. BaseModel CRUD methods route automatically.\n\nTests (tests/core/grpc-transport.test.ts)\n  13 new tests boot a real in-process gRPC server (port 0):\n    • CRUD round-trips: create / findById / findAll / update / delete /\n      count with an in-memory test model\n    • findById returns null for unknown id (same semantics as REST)\n    • 404 RemoteServiceError for unknown model\n    • RemoteService.json transport routing: every REST→gRPC mapping\n      exercised end-to-end through the unified client\n    • internal_secret enforcement: missing secret → 401, correct\n      secret via per-call option succeeds\n\n226/226 total tests pass (was 213). Zero new type errors.\n\nDeps: + @grpc/grpc-js + @grpc/proto-loader (in @buildlish/core)","tree":{"sha":"2acece9b78a6f7ef74601d58c93236e788678e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/2acece9b78a6f7ef74601d58c93236e788678e04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDJlOWY0OGE1OTBkYzE2MDFhYzQwN2M2ZWM0ZmExZjAzZjM0NDdkZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e","sha":"41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e"}],"sha":"2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/2e9f48a590dc1601ac407c6ec4fa1f03f3447dea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T15:14:03Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T15:14:03Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Phase 3d — OpenTelemetry distributed tracing across federation\n\nEvery request now produces a W3C-compliant trace that spans the entire\nfederation: gateway → microservice → saga step → outbound HTTP →\ndownstream service. Traces export to any OTLP-compatible backend\n(Jaeger, Grafana Tempo, Honeycomb, Datadog, New Relic, Lightstep).\nOpen http://localhost:16686 after `docker compose up jaeger` to browse.\n\nObservability module (packages/core/src/observability/)\n  • initTracing({ serviceName, otlpEndpoint, attributes })\n    Idempotent NodeSDK init with auto-instrumentations\n    (http, express, pg, ioredis, fetch, ...). Disables noisy fs\n    instrumentation by default. No-op when no endpoint is configured.\n  • withSpan(name, fn)     async wrapper that auto-closes the span\n                           and records exceptions with ERROR status.\n  • injectTraceContext(headers)   W3C traceparent/tracestate injection\n                                  for any outbound HTTP client.\n  • extractTraceContext(headers, fn)\n                           middleware helper — child spans created\n                           inside fn link to the upstream caller.\n  • getTracer(name)        manual span creation.\n  • getActiveTraceId() / getActiveTraceparent()\n                           current trace id for logs / error bodies.\n\nContext propagation wiring\n  • RemoteService.buildHeaders now injects W3C traceparent on every\n    outgoing call. Each fetch is wrapped in a `remote ${method}\n    ${service}` span with peer.service, http.method, http.status,\n    http.duration_ms, and ERROR status on 5xx.\n  • gatewayProxy extracts the upstream trace before doing anything,\n    then injects W3C traceparent into the proxied request. The full\n    trace tree (upstream → gateway → downstream) appears as one trace\n    in Jaeger.\n  • standalone services do the same extraction in their middleware\n    pipeline so handlers, model calls, and sagas all become child\n    spans automatically.\n  • modules/web/src/server.ts initTracing as the first import and\n    extractTraceContext middleware before any other handlers.\n\nSaga spans (packages/core/src/service/Saga.ts)\n  • Saga.run wraps the entire run in a `saga:${name}` span with\n    buildlish.saga.name and step_count attributes.\n  • Each step is a child span `saga.step:${stepName}` with kind,\n    target service/model, and retry count attributes.\n  • Compensations execute inside the same trace so rollback shows up\n    as a clearly-grouped chain in the trace tree.\n\ndocker-compose.yml\n  • Adds jaegertracing/all-in-one:1.62 service on ports\n    16686 (UI) / 4318 (OTLP HTTP) / 4317 (OTLP gRPC).\n  • Sets OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://jaeger:4318 on the app\n    service so traces flow automatically in dev.\n\nTests (tests/core/observability.test.ts)\n  9 new tests using @opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base InMemorySpanExporter:\n  initTracing idempotency, withSpan OK + ERROR paths, parent/child\n  nesting, injectTraceContext header format, extractTraceContext\n  round-trip preserving trace id, getActiveTraceparent, manual\n  tracer. 213/213 total tests pass (was 204).\n\nDeps\n  + @opentelemetry/api @opentelemetry/sdk-node\n    @opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node\n    @opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-http\n    @opentelemetry/resources @opentelemetry/semantic-conventions\n    @opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base\n  All in @buildlish/core; @opentelemetry/api +\n  @opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base also at root for tests.","tree":{"sha":"e462a8ed5f0e8763be050ce7406ede885192fef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/e462a8ed5f0e8763be050ce7406ede885192fef2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDQxMjkyYjcwZWI1NzFiYThjZjg2NTQ3OWZjYWI4Y2Y1OGU2ZTAyOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78","sha":"36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78"}],"sha":"41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/41292b70eb571ba8cf865479fcab8cf58e6e028e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T14:19:22Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T14:19:22Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Phase 3c — No-code Saga editor + persistent SagaTemplate model\n\nCloses the federation story: users now build distributed transactions\nvisually, run them on demand, and inspect step-by-step results without\nwriting code. Sagas are stored in saga_templates and can be triggered\nby cron jobs, workflows, API calls, or the editor''s \"Test run\" button.\n\nSagaTemplate model (modules/federation/models/SagaTemplate.model.ts)\n  • UUID primary, timestamps, soft-delete, audit, multi-tenant, ACL\n  • code (stable id), name, description, isActive, source enum\n  • definition jsonb — full SagaDefinition matching @buildlish/core types\n  • defaultInput jsonb — merged with per-run input\n  • Stats kept current: runCount, successCount, rollbackCount,\n    lastRunAt, lastSagaId\n  • Indexed by code / isActive / source\n\nFederation module upgrade (modules/federation/)\n  • index.ts is now a real model-bearing module — runs initialize() /\n    generateApis() / seed() lifecycle, registers SagaTemplate\n  • manifest.json updated: models: [''saga_templates'']\n  • views/sagatemplate.views.ts — auto-rendered list + form\n  • menus updated: Federation → Services / Saga Editor / Executions /\n    Saga Templates\n\nRun endpoint (modules/web/src/index.ts)\n  POST /api/v1/saga_templates/:id/run\n    body: { input?, traceId? }\n  Loads the template, validates the definition shape, merges\n  defaultInput + body.input, calls Saga.run(), updates stats\n  (runCount/successCount/rollbackCount/lastRunAt/lastSagaId), and\n  returns the full SagaResult. Rejects when isActive=false.\n\nVisual editor (modules/federation/components/pages/federation_saga_editor.tsx)\n  • Two-pane layout: template sidebar + editor\n  • Per-step builder with Forward / Compensate / retries / backoff\n  • Forward & Compensate ops support three kinds:\n      local   — pick model + op (create/update/delete/findById) + idFrom\n      remote  — pick service (dropdown from /api/v1/services) +\n                method + path\n      custom  — registered factory ref\n  • Input editor (JSON) for each op\n  • Test-run pane: edit input JSON, click Run, see committed vs\n    rolled-back badge, per-step output, error step on failure,\n    one-click copy of saga id (links to Federation → Executions)\n  • Stats inline on each template row (succ/total) and in the header\n\ni18n (en + ar) for all new menu / editor strings.\n\nType-check clean. 204/204 tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"5fdd902125cd23f11eaf92aff250e04e7e706560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/5fdd902125cd23f11eaf92aff250e04e7e706560"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDM2ZDQ3NjhiYzkyNjc0ZDBmMzcxNDRmNWNkMDcyMmQ3ZTQ1ODZmNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5","sha":"5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5"}],"sha":"36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/36d4768bc92674d0f37144f5cd0722d7e4586f78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:57:06Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:57:06Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Phase 3b — Cross-server BaseModel proxy (transparent federation)\n\nCompletes the federation story from Phase 3a. Application code that does\n  await CrmLead.findById(''abc'')\n  await CrmLead.findAll({ where: { status: ''qualified'' } })\n  await CrmLead.create({ name: ''Acme'' })\nnow works **transparently** even when CrmLead lives on a different\nmicroservice — no code changes, no awareness from the caller. The model\nclass can even be a stub; if its table name is registered in\nServiceRegistry, the call HTTP-proxies to the owning service.\n\nNew: RemoteService HTTP client (packages/core/src/service/RemoteService.ts)\n  • Wraps fetch with the same auth headers gatewayProxy uses\n    (x-internal-secret, x-tenant-id, x-user-id, x-company-id,\n     x-department-id, x-branch-id, x-locale, x-permissions, x-groups,\n     x-request-id) so TenantContext propagates across services\n  • Reuses CircuitBreaker (same instance as gatewayProxy) for outgoing\n    calls, with adaptive timeout from the rolling response-time average\n  • RemoteServiceError class with status + parsed body for clean error\n    handling (BaseModel uses it to map 404 → null)\n  • Auto-unwraps the Buildlish { success, data } envelope, but returns\n    raw body for services that don''t follow the convention\n  • Convenience methods: get/post/put/patch/delete + lower-level\n    fetch/json escape hatches\n\nBaseModel routing (packages/core/src/model/BaseModel.ts)\n  Adds a one-line early-return guard at the top of every CRUD method:\n\n    static async findById(id) {\n      const remote = this.getRemoteServiceCode()\n      if (remote) return RemoteService.json(remote, ''GET'', `/api/v1/${table}/${id}`)\n      // ... existing local pipeline unchanged\n    }\n\n  Routes covered:\n    findById → GET    /api/v1/{table}/{id}\n    findAll  → POST   /api/v1/{table}/search   (full QueryOptions payload)\n    create   → POST   /api/v1/{table}\n    update   → PUT    /api/v1/{table}/{id}\n    delete   → DELETE /api/v1/{table}/{id}     (?force=true for hard delete)\n    count    → POST   /api/v1/{table}/count\n    findOne  → delegates through findAll → auto-routes\n\n  Zero performance cost when local — `getRemoteServiceCode()` is a\n  single Map lookup that returns undefined for any unregistered remote.\n  The remote service runs its own ACL / hooks / validation / field\n  security pipeline, so we deliberately skip that on this side — exactly\n  what gatewayProxy already does for incoming requests.\n\nTests (tests/core/remote-routing.test.ts)\n  21 new tests with a stubbed global.fetch + fake ServiceRegistry entry,\n  asserting URL / method / body match the REST convention for every\n  routed method, that 404 maps to null/false where appropriate, that\n  envelope unwrapping works, that local-only models bypass routing,\n  that auth headers are emitted, and that RemoteServiceError surfaces\n  status + parsed body on failures.\n\nTotals: 204/204 tests pass (was 183). Zero new type errors.","tree":{"sha":"a9f120786fbeb24e68581f117b7a9c1a3c1c505c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/a9f120786fbeb24e68581f117b7a9c1a3c1c505c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDVlOWQ5Mzc4YjJmM2M5OWVhYTQwMGI0Yjg1ZDM2ZWU2Y2I1YjQyZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9","sha":"90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9"}],"sha":"5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/5e9d9378b2f3c99eaa400b4b85d36ee6cb5b42d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:28:46Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:28:46Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Phase 3a — Distributed module federation: Saga engine + admin module\n\nThe existing federation infrastructure (ServiceRegistry, gatewayProxy,\nCircuitBreaker, EventBus, standalone services, /internal/services/*) was\nalready substantial. This phase fills the three remaining gaps:\n\n  1. Distributed transactions (the table-stakes feature no other ERP has)\n  2. Public read endpoints for the admin UI\n  3. The admin UI itself\n\nSaga engine (packages/core/src/service/Saga.ts)\n  • Three step kinds: local (in-process model call), remote (HTTP to\n    another registered service), custom (escape hatch)\n  • Sequential forward execution, automatic compensation on failure in\n    reverse order, best-effort compensation chain (one failed comp\n    doesn''t abort the rest)\n  • Retry per step with exponential backoff (maxRetries, backoffMs)\n  • Step input functions receive { ...input, ...previousResults } so\n    later steps can reference earlier outputs\n  • State persisted to Redis (key buildlish:saga:<sagaId>, 7-day TTL)\n    so crashed sagas can be inspected; falls back gracefully without\n    Redis\n  • Reuses ServiceRegistry for remote routing and the same x-internal-\n    secret / x-request-id headers as gatewayProxy — no new transport\n  • Saga.list() and Saga.get() for the admin UI\n\nPublic federation endpoints (modules/web/src/index.ts)\n  • GET /api/v1/services       — service summary, auth-protected\n  • GET /api/v1/sagas?limit=N  — recent saga executions\n  • GET /api/v1/sagas/:id      — single saga full state + step history\n  All three behind apiAuthenticate (the existing JWT middleware), so\n  any logged-in user can read but POST/DELETE remain on /internal/*\n  with the internal secret.\n\nFederation admin module (modules/federation/)\n  Minimal UI-only module (no models). Adds two pages discovered via\n  the existing pageRegistry glob:\n    components/pages/federation_services.tsx\n      Service registry with health badges (healthy / unhealthy /\n      unknown), per-service model lists, registered/last-check times,\n      summary stats, manual refresh.\n    components/pages/federation_sagas.tsx\n      Saga execution list with status filters, click any row to open\n      a sheet showing full input, every step''s result, error message\n      for failed step, compensation markers.\n  Menu under Federation group (Services + Sagas), en + ar i18n.\n\nTests\n  9 saga tests cover happy path, context flow, compensation order,\n  best-effort compensation (continues when one comp throws), steps\n  without compensation, retry success, retry exhaustion, metadata,\n  empty saga. 183/183 total tests pass (was 174).","tree":{"sha":"4bd596d05c18ce1f4c87625508bbb3e3fca070bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/4bd596d05c18ce1f4c87625508bbb3e3fca070bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDkwY2E4MTQ3NDg5N2QxZDM3MjNjNGMwMGFmNGY0MDNjNjQ4N2RlYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc","sha":"5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc"}],"sha":"90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/90ca81474897d1d3723c4c00af4f403c6487dec9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:19:40Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:19:40Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Add customization module — closes the no-code UI customization loop\n\nAdds the backend half of the system shipped in abe8f56. The frontend\nCustomizationPanel already POSTs to /api/v1/customization_manifests with\ngraceful fallback to local-only storage when the endpoint is missing.\nThis module provides the model + auto-generated REST API so manifests\npersist across devices, users, sessions, and tenants.\n\nmodules/customization/\n  manifest.json                        new module, depends on base\n  package.json                         workspace entry\n  index.ts                             CustomizationModule (initialize /\n                                       generateApis / seed lifecycle)\n  models/CustomizationManifest.model.ts\n                                       UUID primary, timestamps, soft-delete,\n                                       audit, multi-tenant, ACL; scoped by\n                                       user / role / company / module with\n                                       priority resolution (50→1000); jsonb\n                                       operations array; source enum\n                                       (manual / imported / ai_generated /\n                                       template); indexed by every scope\n                                       column + priority + active\n  models/index.ts                      registerCustomizationModels()\n  views/customizationmanifest.views.ts list + form, scope-aware filters\n  views/index.ts                       allViews barrel\n  menus/index.ts                       Customizations menu entry\n  i18n/en_US.ts + i18n/ar_SA.ts        English + Arabic translations\n\nmodules/builder/manifest.json\n  Remove data/approval_templates.ts from data array — it''s a TypeScript\n  constants file (exports ApprovalTemplate type definitions), not a\n  Buildlish seed file, so the validator was correctly rejecting it.\n  Fixes the \"data file is missing required model\" startup warning.\n\nAll 174 tests still pass. Zero new type errors.","tree":{"sha":"54ac58e93fa499d597dee397d3a56132f63c0fc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/54ac58e93fa499d597dee397d3a56132f63c0fc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc","node_id":"C_kwDOSE_BdtoAKDVlNzkwMmVlMDA4ZWZiMmMzYWI0ZjUzM2MyYTUyNWMwZTEzMzM3YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/buildlish/buildlish/commit/f4b8ca6532216fc4252f72ae5921c8c588e88535","sha":"f4b8ca6532216fc4252f72ae5921c8c588e88535","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/f4b8ca6532216fc4252f72ae5921c8c588e88535"}],"sha":"5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/5e7902ee008efb2c3ab4f533c2a525c0e13337bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thesyedyahya","id":106922377,"login":"thesyedyahya","node_id":"U_kgDOBl-BiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/commits/f4b8ca6532216fc4252f72ae5921c8c588e88535/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:13:50Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T13:13:50Z","email":"thesyedyahya@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Syed Yahya"},"message":"Add no-code UI customization system with portable manifest format\n\nBuilds a persistent customization layer on top of the existing\nComponentRegistry so non-developers can replace, extend, restyle, inject,\nhide, or reconfigure any UI element from a single in-app panel — no code\nchanges, scoped per tenant / role / user / module / company.\n\nCore (modules/web/core/customization/):\n  - types.ts                       portable JSON manifest format (replace,\n                                   extend, classOverride, slot, propsOverride,\n                                   hide, styleVar ops + wrapper recipes)\n  - VariantLibrary                 registry of pre-built component variants\n                                   modules can publish for users to pick from\n  - ClassOverrideManager           runtime Tailwind class injection via\n                                   MutationObserver on data-component-key\n  - PropsOverrideRegistry          patches default props by key+scope; merged\n                                   inside useComponent so any registered\n                                   component picks them up automatically\n  - wrappers.tsx                   declarative wrapper recipes\n                                   (banner, tooltip, badge, card, padding,\n                                   conditional, wrapElement, custom) plus\n                                   registerWrapperRecipe for new ones\n  - CustomizationLoader            translates manifest ops into the right\n                                   ComponentRegistry / manager calls,\n                                   supports apply / revert / hot-swap\n\nStore (modules/web/stores/customization.ts):\n  - Zustand store with backend sync to /api/v1/customization_manifests\n  - Draft state with optimistic updates, persisted across reloads\n  - Save / delete / toggle / reapply, all live-applied without reload\n\nUI (modules/web/components/customization/):\n  - CustomizationPanel       single Sheet with three tabs (Manifests,\n                             Editor, Inspect) — the only entry point users\n                             ever need\n  - OperationEditor          per-op visual editor with autocomplete from\n                             ComponentRegistry and VariantLibrary\n  - CustomizationToggleButton drop-in button for any toolbar\n\nWiring:\n  - main.tsx mounts CustomizationInitializer (loads manifests on auth)\n    and CustomizationPanel at the root\n  - useComponent now merges PropsOverrideRegistry props before render so\n    propsOverride operations take effect automatically\n\nBrand themes (modules/web/stores/brandThemes.ts):\n  - 14 brand-grade theme presets (Linear, Stripe, Vercel, Notion, Apple,\n    Cursor, Arc, Enterprise — light + dark variants) merged into the\n    existing theme store preset list\n\nAll 174 tests still pass. Zero new type errors.","tree":{"sha":"481a411493a516e298d1091fb1086994911de1db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/trees/481a411493a516e298d1091fb1086994911de1db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buildlish/buildlish/git/commits/f4b8ca6532216fc4252f72ae5921c8c588e88535","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106922377?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thesyedyahya/even