ved_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzolotar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzolotar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzolotar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzolotar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzolotar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nzolotar/nzolotar/commits/bf026afcf1a4d6152301eedda26c01915e1f6e13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-20T01:28:40Z","email":"nzolotar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nat"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-20T01:28:40Z","email":"nzolotar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nat"},"message":"Add deduplication library with three strategies\n\nIntroduce a deduplication library with in-memory, database,\nand Azure Service Bus strategies. Define a shared interface\n(`IDeduplicator`) and implement each strategy in its own class\n(`InMemoryDeduplicator`, `DatabaseDeduplicator`, and\n`ServiceBusDeduplicator`).\n\nAdd demos (`InMemoryDemo`, `DatabaseDemo`) and tests for each\nstrategy, covering key scenarios like duplicate detection,\npersistence, TTL handling, and concurrency. Use EF Core with\nSQLite for the database strategy and `IMemoryCache` for the\nin-memory strategy. Structure the solution with a main project\n(`DeduplicationStore`) and a test project (`DeduplicationStore.Tests`).\n\nUpdate `Program.cs` to showcase deduplication demos. Include\nsupporting files like `DeduplicationDbContext`, `ProcessedMessage`\nentity, and project configurations targeting .NET 9.0.","tree":{"sha":"b3d72035a8d12dc26afae594f493f5d0ad58aba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nzolotar/nzolotar/git/trees/b3d72035a8d12dc26afae594f493f5d0ad58aba3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nzolotar/nzolotar/git/commits/bf026afcf1a4d6152301eedda26c01915e1f6e13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"ver