rnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/757fc55f6ecad5eeccfd9b396f2a9fa87d1bb7b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T19:44:44Z","email":"ed.barnes937@gmail.com","name":"ed-barnes937"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T19:44:58Z","email":"ed.barnes937@gmail.com","name":"ed-barnes937"},"message":"feat: replace per-lens recording config with workspace focus scope\n\nMoves \"which recording am I looking at\" from a per-panel picker\n(config.recordingId + updatePanelConfig mutations) to a single\nworkspace-level focus scope dimension (scope_type=''recording'').\n\n- Scope/ScopeDim types gain recordingId; decodeScope maps it\n- useRecordings(courseTag?) accepts an optional course filter\n- DrawerSidebar ScopeEditor grows a Recording picker (shown only\n  when a recording-consuming lens is on the canvas)\n- TopBar scope chip resolves and shows the focused recording title\n- setScope server mutation atomically clears any recording scope\n  when the course changes, preventing torn {new course, stale\n  recording} state (B4 invariant)\n- Transcript, AudioCapture, Connections lenses read scope.recordingId;\n  in-panel pickers and orphaned useRecordings() calls removed\n- Manifests for all three lenses declare filters: [''recordingId'']\n- Simulator setScope mirrors the B4 invariant for test parity\n- IWFT tests move recordingId from config to scope\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9b47ef74fda6d4631bc47946414f530a760c19c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/d9b47ef74fda6d4631bc47946414f530a760c19c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/757fc55f6ecad5eeccfd9b396f2a9fa87d1bb7b3","verification":{"payload":"tree d9b47ef74fda6d4631bc47946414f530a760c19c\nparent e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc\nauthor ed-barnes937 <ed.barnes937@gmail.com> 1781034284 +0100\ncommitter ed-barnes937 <ed.barnes937@gmail.com> 1781034298 +0100\n\nfeat: replace per-lens recording config with workspace focus scope\n\nMoves \"which recording am I looking at\" from a per-panel picker\n(config.recordingId + updatePanelConfig mutations) to a single\nworkspace-level focus scope dimension (scope_type=''recording'').\n\n- Scope/ScopeDim types gain recordingId; decodeScope maps it\n- useRecordings(courseTag?) accepts an optional course filter\n- DrawerSidebar ScopeEditor grows a Recording picker (shown only\n  when a recording-consuming lens is on the canvas)\n- TopBar scope chip resolves and shows the focused recording title\n- setScope server mutation atomically clears any recording scope\n  when the course changes, preventing torn {new course, stale\n  recording} state (B4 invariant)\n- Transcript, AudioCapture, Connections lenses read scope.recordingId;\n  in-panel pickers and orphaned useRecordings() calls removed\n- Manifests for all three lenses declare filters: [''recordingId'']\n- Simulator setScope mirrors the B4 invariant for test parity\n- IWFT tests move recordingId from config to scope\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJmMnMo+g5uW8W5iOsW47KBYBav\nV7aHCuW21+sEK//6YAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCO7B1kUwuTgtMjpD/hFNrds6UTLppSwCq6t5AiAEaIEEaI2O2JJFZkIwpeff8wMbn\n1pJfvJpuDNs63xnpdU1A8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-09T19:45:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/757fc55f6ecad5eeccfd9b396f2a9fa87d1bb7b3","node_id":"C_kwDOSFtkOtoAKDc1N2ZjNTVmNmVjYWQ1ZWVjY2ZkOWIzOTZmMmE5ZmE4N2QxYmI3YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc","sha":"e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc"}],"sha":"757fc55f6ecad5eeccfd9b396f2a9fa87d1bb7b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/757fc55f6ecad5eeccfd9b396f2a9fa87d1bb7b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:09:49Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:09:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: repair e2e suite after freeform-canvas migration (#55)\n\nThe smoke/panels/workspace/journey e2e files predated the freeform-canvas\nrewrite (migration 006) and targeted the removed react-grid-layout UI, so\nthe suite could not pass. Repairs:\n\n- PanelGridPom: rewrite on canvas-container / data-panel-id / panel-title\n  testids; expectEmpty now uses the workspace-empty-state testid\n- PanelContainerPom: panel-header is the drag handle, removal is the\n  \"Close <title>\" button, automations via \"Automations for <label>\"\n- smoke: assert top-bar + canvas-container instead of the long-gone\n  ''Malleable PLS'' string\n- default workspace is In Lecture (store inits to ws-in-lecture): tests\n  that relied on Evening Review being active at load now switch to it\n  explicitly; panels/workspace default-state assertions updated\n- gap-analysis panel title is its manifest label ''All Courses'', not\n  ''Gap Analysis''\n- journey-1: the \"Recording complete … total\" block is hidden below the\n  @tall container-query breakpoint at the seeded 240px panel height;\n  assert the picker value + visible timer instead\n- rate limiter: DISABLE_RATE_LIMIT=1 opt-out wired into the Playwright\n  webServer so full-suite runs don''t trip the 100 req/min limit as\n  silent 429s\n\nGate: PG_PORT=5444 API_PORT=3011 WEB_PORT=5183 pnpm test:e2e — 18/18\ngreen twice in a row from a cold start (docker compose down between\nruns). typecheck / 305 vitest / 52 CT unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b280483118726cf296477da05551745dd34ca0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/5b280483118726cf296477da05551745dd34ca0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b280483118726cf296477da05551745dd34ca0d\nparent 5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531\nauthor Ed Barnes <Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com> 1780610989 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780610989 +0100\n\nfix: repair e2e suite after freeform-canvas migration (#55)\n\nThe smoke/panels/workspace/journey e2e files predated the freeform-canvas\nrewrite (migration 006) and targeted the removed react-grid-layout UI, so\nthe suite could not pass. Repairs:\n\n- PanelGridPom: rewrite on canvas-container / data-panel-id / panel-title\n  testids; expectEmpty now uses the workspace-empty-state testid\n- PanelContainerPom: panel-header is the drag handle, removal is the\n  \"Close <title>\" button, automations via \"Automations for <label>\"\n- smoke: assert top-bar + canvas-container instead of the long-gone\n  ''Malleable PLS'' string\n- default workspace is In Lecture (store inits to ws-in-lecture): tests\n  that relied on Evening Review being active at load now switch to it\n  explicitly; panels/workspace default-state assertions updated\n- gap-analysis panel title is its manifest label ''All Courses'', not\n  ''Gap Analysis''\n- journey-1: the \"Recording complete … total\" block is hidden below the\n  @tall container-query breakpoint at the seeded 240px panel height;\n  assert the picker value + visible timer instead\n- rate limiter: DISABLE_RATE_LIMIT=1 opt-out wired into the Playwright\n  webServer so full-suite runs don''t trip the 100 req/min limit as\n  silent 429s\n\nGate: PG_PORT=5444 API_PORT=3011 WEB_PORT=5183 pnpm test:e2e — 18/18\ngreen twice in a row from a cold start (docker compose down between\nruns). typecheck / 305 vitest / 52 CT unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIfetCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM9cQAFbNBKEvZEuJn+APYg7Pb3BR\npcuoImBBcApnzHn+SThDOsJrLHLTS8dQU91HwY/OrZYUDyntr7c7gBoK796cNUm+\nMUOtbhZfnh6BfP+cjOylKJ6pveeOx0U+j90s9RsBQew8PJzFNZ2fZefyrkuDuMbf\n6uE3LGenF0Vz8Rzy1ZsGvlFPy/DC5dBVJ8OmwmvXc76ciK1vJJaOYz16agiF4tJn\n4SpsnOjDTQd0fNhZ+DKd/39KgrM+jMYODDmKpUPOZ3KDNNB9QPM5CaDokofeeMYZ\nCKEqhnOv+nC69jD8yZHmonvsXP3MnY8OcQDE1mc+ewdh0JUnJyTjgV0TkBNuLs+H\nj3nM+vEgvUF6eGBTJk4bYGqonSKT/hD5qhrHKrK/xhCRMVs/NXetcna+bKycVFP6\nBAzYS8DWkMkaA+Tu/ssQKcBbhKUyG3t1IlMAlZEBd7fqmTLxaTK6oyq5LKwa6/Xr\ndeInC3ypSNI5p19LxhwxIK8UUPGRZ7lTWtRtjPiRn2BqjpdorBsjPeMwNVunQ1ZJ\nw4ykvQTZMB77kqHtCxIbMcXY64bgV4IJt+U1SxwzO0niFKnCOD3aBoiWT94q13Yq\n2C+KZ+n48DyUphqZDs/5qMn4dFtJlsIGKgo3YXDUTBRAaMt/izYshFbw8eVtuM3Y\nLPOU/IkdGORyfRWuPEqs\n=hotA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-04T22:09:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc","node_id":"C_kwDOSFtkOtoAKGU2NTNhZjZlM2VmMTdiNmY0MTJhYmM0ODU1NzMzMTM3M2MzNWQ0ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531","sha":"5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531"}],"sha":"e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/e653af6e3ef17b6f412abc48557331373c35d4fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T21:47:52Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T21:47:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: Tier 4 dedup sweeps — server, shared-ui, lenses, test infra (#54)\n\nServer (apps/server):\n- Shared recordingScope schema in routers/_shared.ts; delete dead\n  courseTag/timeframe fields from tags/annotations/confidence/aggregates\n  inputs (and the client callsites that sent them); drop weeklyOverview''s\n  unused input\n- Delete Context.withTenant (byte-identical to withUser) — all 42 router\n  callsites now call withUser(ctx.userId, ...); Context shrinks to {userId}\n- Extract insertWorkflowJob() + workflowJobsJson() SQL fragment, deduping\n  3x job-insert loops and 3x json_agg projections\n- Pin panel config to jsonb object end-to-end: addPanel input becomes\n  z.record, dead typeof-string branches deleted (server, client, simulator,\n  seed data), WorkspacePanel.config typed as Record<string, unknown>\n- ai:transcribe mock path throws on missing _userId instead of reporting\n  fake success\n- Document single-process limits of the in-memory rate limiter and SSE bus\n\nshared-ui / workspace-shell:\n- New Select (chevron baked in) and TextField primitives; replace 4\n  divergent copy-pasted field-class sites\n- Delete RecordingPicker from shared-ui (domain logic in generic package);\n  both lens consumers inline Select directly\n- Extract <WorkflowList> load/error/empty scaffold shared by\n  WorkflowSettingsPanel and LensAutomationsButton\n- Export formatTime(ms) from shared-ui; dedupe 2 copies + TestMeLens''s\n  seconds-based inline variant\n- Dialog body uses surface tokens (bg-surface-raised/border-border-subtle)\n  so it follows the light theme; backdrop scrim intentionally stays black\n- Resolve 8 duplicate test suites per-component: Vitest+RTL for pure-render\n  components + Dialog (its Playwright CT suite was already broken — portal\n  renders outside the CT component root), Playwright CT for Switch;\n  missing cases ported before deletion\n\nLenses:\n- Extract useAudioRecorder() and useAudioPlayback() from AudioCaptureLens;\n  playback progress now driven by the real audio element''s timeupdate\n  events instead of a parallel 1s setInterval that could desync\n- Typed vite-env.d.ts ImportMetaEnv declarations; remove all\n  (import.meta as any) casts\n\nTest infra:\n- DialogPom takes Page directly; drop unused titleText and the broken\n  Page/Locator discriminator\n- playwright webServer now boots postgres (docker --wait) + migrations +\n  API server + Vite — e2e runs from a cold start with only docker; new\n  unauthenticated /health endpoint; PG_PORT/API_PORT/WEB_PORT overridable\n  so parallel worktrees don''t collide; ALLOWED_ORIGINS threaded through\n- scope.e2e.ts uses TopBarPom.openDrawer()/switchToWorkspace() instead of\n  local raw-selector helpers\n- New root typecheck script (tsc -p apps/web && tsc -p apps/server) — none\n  existed; fixes the pre-existing errors it surfaced (rotted deep import,\n  missing sort_order in simulator seeds, WorkflowCard workspace_id typing)\n\nOut of scope, noted for follow-up: C4 (ConnectionsLens CONCEPT_SEGMENTS\nresolution needs schema/endpoint design); the pre-canvas e2e tests (smoke,\npanels, workspace, journeys) target the old react-grid-layout UI and were\nalready failing before this change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e0dff01bc60d176c81dbccaba1c8f6a39eac3c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/3e0dff01bc60d176c81dbccaba1c8f6a39eac3c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e0dff01bc60d176c81dbccaba1c8f6a39eac3c3\nparent dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d\nauthor Ed Barnes <Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com> 1780609672 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780609672 +0100\n\nrefactor: Tier 4 dedup sweeps — server, shared-ui, lenses, test infra (#54)\n\nServer (apps/server):\n- Shared recordingScope schema in routers/_shared.ts; delete dead\n  courseTag/timeframe fields from tags/annotations/confidence/aggregates\n  inputs (and the client callsites that sent them); drop weeklyOverview''s\n  unused input\n- Delete Context.withTenant (byte-identical to withUser) — all 42 router\n  callsites now call withUser(ctx.userId, ...); Context shrinks to {userId}\n- Extract insertWorkflowJob() + workflowJobsJson() SQL fragment, deduping\n  3x job-insert loops and 3x json_agg projections\n- Pin panel config to jsonb object end-to-end: addPanel input becomes\n  z.record, dead typeof-string branches deleted (server, client, simulator,\n  seed data), WorkspacePanel.config typed as Record<string, unknown>\n- ai:transcribe mock path throws on missing _userId instead of reporting\n  fake success\n- Document single-process limits of the in-memory rate limiter and SSE bus\n\nshared-ui / workspace-shell:\n- New Select (chevron baked in) and TextField primitives; replace 4\n  divergent copy-pasted field-class sites\n- Delete RecordingPicker from shared-ui (domain logic in generic package);\n  both lens consumers inline Select directly\n- Extract <WorkflowList> load/error/empty scaffold shared by\n  WorkflowSettingsPanel and LensAutomationsButton\n- Export formatTime(ms) from shared-ui; dedupe 2 copies + TestMeLens''s\n  seconds-based inline variant\n- Dialog body uses surface tokens (bg-surface-raised/border-border-subtle)\n  so it follows the light theme; backdrop scrim intentionally stays black\n- Resolve 8 duplicate test suites per-component: Vitest+RTL for pure-render\n  components + Dialog (its Playwright CT suite was already broken — portal\n  renders outside the CT component root), Playwright CT for Switch;\n  missing cases ported before deletion\n\nLenses:\n- Extract useAudioRecorder() and useAudioPlayback() from AudioCaptureLens;\n  playback progress now driven by the real audio element''s timeupdate\n  events instead of a parallel 1s setInterval that could desync\n- Typed vite-env.d.ts ImportMetaEnv declarations; remove all\n  (import.meta as any) casts\n\nTest infra:\n- DialogPom takes Page directly; drop unused titleText and the broken\n  Page/Locator discriminator\n- playwright webServer now boots postgres (docker --wait) + migrations +\n  API server + Vite — e2e runs from a cold start with only docker; new\n  unauthenticated /health endpoint; PG_PORT/API_PORT/WEB_PORT overridable\n  so parallel worktrees don''t collide; ALLOWED_ORIGINS threaded through\n- scope.e2e.ts uses TopBarPom.openDrawer()/switchToWorkspace() instead of\n  local raw-selector helpers\n- New root typecheck script (tsc -p apps/web && tsc -p apps/server) — none\n  existed; fixes the pre-existing errors it surfaced (rotted deep import,\n  missing sort_order in simulator seeds, WorkflowCard workspace_id typing)\n\nOut of scope, noted for follow-up: C4 (ConnectionsLens CONCEPT_SEGMENTS\nresolution needs schema/endpoint design); the pre-canvas e2e tests (smoke,\npanels, workspace, journeys) target the old react-grid-layout UI and were\nalready failing before this change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nw