":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d","sha":"dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d"}],"sha":"5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/5a9fe48648c0d3869a5233abbfb09a74c959b531"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T15:32:18Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T15:32:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: Tier 3 structural extractions (geometry, sync hooks, substrate types) (#53)\n\n* refactor(panel-system): extract geometry helpers and usePanelDrag\n\nPulls the untested clamp/resize math out of CanvasEngine into pure,\nunit-tested functions in geometry.ts. ResizeHandle and the new usePanelDrag\nhook consume these functions directly, so DraggablePanel shrinks from ~190\nlines to ~60 wiring lines with no behavior change.\n\n- geometry.ts: clampToCanvas, resizeDimensions, anchoredPosition (18 tests)\n- usePanelDrag: owns motion values, isGesturing, and all drag handlers\n- Snap ordering preserved: snap-then-clamp in both handleDrag and handleDragEnd\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(workspace-shell): extract sync hooks and shared scope decoder\n\nPulls the two state-machine effects out of WorkspaceShell (405→260 lines)\nand centralises the scope decode logic that was duplicated across three files.\n\n- usePanelSync: owns syncedWorkspaceRef, full-vs-incremental DB→canvas sync\n- useWorkspaceBackgroundSync: owns both background effects and prevBgRef\n- decodeScope: added to @pls/substrate-client; replaces scopesFromDb in\n  WorkspaceShell and the inline scope_type===''tag'' lookups in DrawerSidebar\n  and TopBar\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(substrate-client): type workflow/job hooks, delete consumer casts\n\nAnnotates useWorkflowsForWorkspace, useWorkflowsForLens, and useRecentJobs\nwith explicit domain return types (WorkflowWithJobs[], JobRun[]). Removes\nthe resulting consumer casts in WorkflowSettingsPanel, LensAutomationsButton,\nand JobStatusIndicator. Three contained casts remain at the hook level\ninstead of five scattered across consumers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: update lockfile for substrate-client @pls/workflows dep\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fba43ff8f36c13e378cb0342c2fc3c5a7dfd3d1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/fba43ff8f36c13e378cb0342c2fc3c5a7dfd3d1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d","verification":{"payload":"tree fba43ff8f36c13e378cb0342c2fc3c5a7dfd3d1b\nparent a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff\nauthor Ed Barnes <Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com> 1780587138 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780587138 +0100\n\nrefactor: Tier 3 structural extractions (geometry, sync hooks, substrate types) (#53)\n\n* refactor(panel-system): extract geometry helpers and usePanelDrag\n\nPulls the untested clamp/resize math out of CanvasEngine into pure,\nunit-tested functions in geometry.ts. ResizeHandle and the new usePanelDrag\nhook consume these functions directly, so DraggablePanel shrinks from ~190\nlines to ~60 wiring lines with no behavior change.\n\n- geometry.ts: clampToCanvas, resizeDimensions, anchoredPosition (18 tests)\n- usePanelDrag: owns motion values, isGesturing, and all drag handlers\n- Snap ordering preserved: snap-then-clamp in both handleDrag and handleDragEnd\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(workspace-shell): extract sync hooks and shared scope decoder\n\nPulls the two state-machine effects out of WorkspaceShell (405→260 lines)\nand centralises the scope decode logic that was duplicated across three files.\n\n- usePanelSync: owns syncedWorkspaceRef, full-vs-incremental DB→canvas sync\n- useWorkspaceBackgroundSync: owns both background effects and prevBgRef\n- decodeScope: added to @pls/substrate-client; replaces scopesFromDb in\n  WorkspaceShell and the inline scope_type===''tag'' lookups in DrawerSidebar\n  and TopBar\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(substrate-client): type workflow/job hooks, delete consumer casts\n\nAnnotates useWorkflowsForWorkspace, useWorkflowsForLens, and useRecentJobs\nwith explicit domain return types (WorkflowWithJobs[], JobRun[]). Removes\nthe resulting consumer casts in WorkflowSettingsPanel, LensAutomationsButton,\nand JobStatusIndicator. Three contained casts remain at the hook level\ninstead of five scattered across consumers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: update lockfile for substrate-client @pls/workflows dep\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIZqCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABpYQAGZo0twDwLmFLrp+i05iGIXw\niUrRNsHNdwGSMvfcBOZsC1N0bBGmVkA404szgsqkkx14ogu40Pp61H05eUrfdXZk\nMDSJzL0HXg28z9s3Jos7uWmcbMaUkBqna3Yr24dziRcSr9na1sPLIzRYRdcmWyK5\nNvGvlFNXS8W/G3has81kCUETD6V8sX7BL9dSim/DeT2AprO/NpNPJyMNxJXvqDmn\nSJvrHtQQihq59+1/LQUNsFloA0TK9Ck1gV/E0DFbgDhPdm5e46Yi58Jt+Iou8EJm\nIEaaaxOJdj2VqANsYZCV993Z3EZtM97VB+qNBwCpCyZnuFOH829tMpePVjHFnKP2\nvnQXd99TRI5mLfhxMvPWvMFDCG+KZbwuqc+Oixsa7PFy4JPvO0VByQr4cUYqWpSL\nXW2AYsqkc5EhrbSSM01k+D00QGVr4/PiXxgFF4Wai8OkmTuoJUFane72TA6XErs1\npXO+5t2st0Ye7pU9+xYxm3MhYTZyRey7PVSyB32gI/yjXaGRvufh/CdQHVie761e\nAY7HwBdceqfJ0uoa3sMwlr+Ol3ae7g5dyZlm5QzPyNVi7nKI1QzilCYSfFTjNcV3\nj9WtqT2BJHMvykJ55v63ALLb3AFIODPxQux5GLmMBRN0MkxVszDsPUM05m/56m5u\nyBu20x1v9W6ujCzjkDYk\n=lkJC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-04T15:32:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d","node_id":"C_kwDOSFtkOtoAKGRjYTExNWFmZTZkZjQ1ZDI4NzUzYTE1ODcxOWRiZTAwYTJiMzRjM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff","sha":"a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff"}],"sha":"dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/dca115afe6df45d28753a158719dbe00a2b34c3d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T13:58:41Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T13:58:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: delete sql.js runtime, dead surface & simulator EndpointBehaviour (#52)\n\n* chore: delete sql.js runtime, dead surface, and simulator EndpointBehaviour (#tier2)\n\nPart A — shrinks @pls/substrate to types + QUESTIONS + 3 static metadata\nhelpers. Deletes ~1400 lines: all of queries/, hooks/, db.ts, schema.ts,\nseed.ts, sql.js.d.ts, sql-js-adapter + test, sql-wasm.wasm, and removes\nsql.js / @tanstack/react-query / react deps. WorkflowWithJobs re-exported\nfrom @pls/workflows (canonical shape).\n\nPart B — deletes EndpointBehaviour subsystem (zero test coverage); moves\nWorkflow/WorkflowJob/JobRun type definitions into in-memory-db.ts to\ndecouple simulator from substrate; adds simulator-parity.test.ts (20 read\nprocedures, 2 missing procedures documented as failing). Seed unification\nleft as TODO in reseed.ts — panel positions already differ between SQL\nand TS seeds.\n\nPart C — dead-surface sweep: LensMeta, LensCategory ''both'', meta? on\nLensLoader, defaultSize on PanelManifest, useTagsForTarget/useDeleteTag\nfrom SubstrateReader/Writer and substrate-trpc, toggleFocusMode action + 4\ntests, usePanelPulse hook, vestigial panelId/dbPanelId/onRemove props on\nPanelContainer, dead cn import in WeeklyOverviewLens.\n\nAll 292 tests pass; zero tsc errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* updated lockfile\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0082f6330e30e4c6b578cfb9f58961c9264e088e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/0082f6330e30e4c6b578cfb9f58961c9264e088e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff","verification":{"payloa