0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/a0e585e350e758411c5d82bc32bfba6044f7c1ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/6dbb6410116ada2f77940edbd27f03cf7a9e0308/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T13:14:33Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T13:14:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: pg override dedup, atomic job claim, delete panel-demo (#51)\n\n* fix: correctness fixes — pg override dedup, atomic job claim, panel-demo\n\nIssue 1: getEffectiveWorkflows in the pg adapter now uses DISTINCT ON with\nworkspace_id NULLS LAST to enforce the same override-wins rule as the sql.js\nreference (packages/substrate/src/queries/workflows.ts). A default + workspace\noverride for the same (source_lens, condition_field, condition_value) previously\ndouble-dispatched; now only the override is returned.\n\nIssue 2: claimPendingJobRuns is now an atomic UPDATE … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\nthat flips status to ''running'' in the same statement, preventing concurrent\nworkers from double-claiming. The server job-runner drops the outer sql.begin\n(adapter now manages its own short per-call transactions), so pooled connections\nare no longer held across multi-second executor I/O. Core runner skips the\nredundant updateJobRunStatus(''running'') call when the adapter has already claimed\natomically (detected via job.status === ''running'' on the returned row).\n\nIssue 3: Delete apps/panel-demo (broken — imported PanelGrid/PanelGridItem that\nnever existed) and the dead Panel/PanelProps components from packages/panel-system\nwhose only consumer was the demo. Production uses CanvasEngine + PanelChrome.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: ignore .claude/ directory\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"293cd5210da03a6c13494d018072f411b1d0bf69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/293cd5210da03a6c13494d018072f411b1d0bf69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/6dbb6410116ada2f77940edbd27f03cf7a9e0308","verification":{"payload":"tree 293cd5210da03a6c13494d018072f411b1d0bf69\nparent d396f9b39e07ddf44efb9c364e9ac0227f997caf\nauthor Ed Barnes <Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com> 1780578873 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780578873 +0100\n\nfix: pg override dedup, atomic job claim, delete panel-demo (#51)\n\n* fix: correctness fixes — pg override dedup, atomic job claim, panel-demo\n\nIssue 1: getEffectiveWorkflows in the pg adapter now uses DISTINCT ON with\nworkspace_id NULLS LAST to enforce the same override-wins rule as the sql.js\nreference (packages/substrate/src/queries/workflows.ts). A default + workspace\noverride for the same (source_lens, condition_field, condition_value) previously\ndouble-dispatched; now only the override is returned.\n\nIssue 2: claimPendingJobRuns is now an atomic UPDATE … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\nthat flips status to ''running'' in the same statement, preventing concurrent\nworkers from double-claiming. The server job-runner drops the outer sql.begin\n(adapter now manages its own short per-call transactions), so pooled connections\nare no longer held across multi-second executor I/O. Core runner skips the\nredundant updateJobRunStatus(''running'') call when the adapter has already claimed\natomically (detected via job.status === ''running'' on the returned row).\n\nIssue 3: Delete apps/panel-demo (broken — imported PanelGrid/PanelGridItem that\nnever existed) and the dead Panel/PanelProps components from packages/panel-system\nwhose only consumer was the demo. Production uses CanvasEngine + PanelChrome.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: ignore .claude/ directory\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIXo5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6P0QAF8yKLWwCOuy/gAeyaRTPD3j\nhJGdC56RLR0WmxiYjH1oqaS0x/z6XdsOQykl02FiVjMAdkW1yqVQkPNU8aB1TlXV\n2iBCfCDXEGh/p3zK2oZ0tBSXYVKfSHmnLP4uSnyKLCZ3mM6G8OOHtKJ5c+dPidiS\neDdjwxByzi79pCVZRyExmgv+CqxezkrVFlRCOTSVK8alQdYC6j/6iT5FS5L/KYs0\nkcB7dJtPoz2jcp7OsQyL7ImqfWpNbi0+Q7pBstmBbx6aRnAFJY4U2iNYAUWIVy1G\nLlBja46zrlvgpeGjhDTWdbx6C5kq6vWTIIiyPH64rkEuIFH7L9jFJXTNv/TrblkE\nSDnNw3VxLMs1ziPVRuNRp05NGirbyWNxjWkAEbZR1CR9cu0C5I6VEsGB4gC7bo9d\nhfb3CvBFxaQVv+yK2E9+n3Ad6MwTfK1b4DXapc7EwJDLZpPI3VRId9No/ghn11NR\n74GamOdQk7PvFtN7dwL85Ncwym/xiaE6YfVIgAF/Cvl6Zh5lSzqxi0UWE3dpqnpS\n84sB5lMwobisUv29Qs9ncIoJUl/bqQwicp48T6YSyruwDrvzZ3Y6dNb51tJgFd1z\nbZ5DA74AKNERtZzM0oHkSEHAm+imCJCx6a4kkHDX3AP3oKpTYJhpA6n6CiH+iAw7\nM2u20b8guqiYkwqxHJ2v\n=eESI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE----