mMDk3ZDg0NzE3NDE4NDg5ZGVjODljNjc3Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/72ee9eefca09b66994b4d2b7aa601c87fdc3b4c3","sha":"72ee9eefca09b66994b4d2b7aa601c87fdc3b4c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/72ee9eefca09b66994b4d2b7aa601c87fdc3b4c3"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9","sha":"7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9"}],"sha":"7b157a0d5fd6df097d84717418489dec89c67779","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/7b157a0d5fd6df097d84717418489dec89c67779"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:44:36Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:44:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(scope): drop obsolete recording scope row, rewrite scope e2e (#47)\n\nThird and final PR of the workspace-scope rethink — data cleanup and e2e\ncoverage for the new model.\n\nMigration:\n- New `009_drop_scope_recording.sql` deletes `workspace_scopes` rows of\n  type `recording` (now meaningless — recordingId moved to per-panel config).\n- Removed the matching `ws-in-lecture/recording/rec-bio-4` row from the\n  seed in `002_seed.sql`. The in-lecture target lives on each panel''s\n  `config.recordingId` (already in `008_seed_panels.sql`).\n\nE2E coverage:\n- Rewrote `e2e/scope.e2e.ts` to assert per-workspace behaviour:\n  - In Lecture renders no Scope section\n  - Evening Review renders Course + Timeframe, no Recording picker\n  - Changing course / timeframe persists\n- Tests switch workspaces via the TopBar''s `WorkspaceSwitcher` (workspaces\n  haven''t lived in the drawer aside for a while — see follow-up below).\n\nPOM:\n- Dropped `recordingSelect` and `selectRecording` from `SidebarPom`.\n- `scopeSection` now targets the new `data-testid=\"scope-section\"` and\n  returns 0 nodes when the section is hidden (e.g. In Lecture).\n- Selects are found by accessible name via new `aria-label`s on the\n  Course / Timeframe selects in `DrawerSidebar`.\n\nOut of scope (pre-existing staleness):\n- `SidebarPom.workspaceButtons`, `switchToWorkspace`, `deleteWorkspace`,\n  etc. still point at the aside, but `WorkspaceSwitcher` has lived in\n  TopBar for a while. Journey tests depend on these — left as-is; worth\n  a separate cleanup.\n\nTest plan:\n- `pnpm test` — 281/281 passing\n- `tsc` clean on new code\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14eca3aace20541bc89256e372c1689ce7b04033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/14eca3aace20541bc89256e372c1689ce7b04033"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9","verification":{"payload":"tree 14eca3aace20541bc89256e372c1689ce7b04033\nparent 8d501b24db54a53d38a92227f4a97b253e43493e\nauthor Ed Barnes <Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com> 1780177476 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780177476 +0100\n\nchore(scope): drop obsolete recording scope row, rewrite scope e2e (#47)\n\nThird and final PR of the workspace-scope rethink — data cleanup and e2e\ncoverage for the new model.\n\nMigration:\n- New `009_drop_scope_recording.sql` deletes `workspace_scopes` rows of\n  type `recording` (now meaningless — recordingId moved to per-panel config).\n- Removed the matching `ws-in-lecture/recording/rec-bio-4` row from the\n  seed in `002_seed.sql`. The in-lecture target lives on each panel''s\n  `config.recordingId` (already in `008_seed_panels.sql`).\n\nE2E coverage:\n- Rewrote `e2e/scope.e2e.ts` to assert per-workspace behaviour:\n  - In Lecture renders no Scope section\n  - Evening Review renders Course + Timeframe, no Recording picker\n  - Changing course / timeframe persists\n- Tests switch workspaces via the TopBar''s `WorkspaceSwitcher` (workspaces\n  haven''t lived in the drawer aside for a while — see follow-up below).\n\nPOM:\n- Dropped `recordingSelect` and `selectRecording` from `SidebarPom`.\n- `scopeSection` now targets the new `data-testid=\"scope-section\"` and\n  returns 0 nodes when the section is hidden (e.g. In Lecture).\n- Selects are found by accessible name via new `aria-label`s on the\n  Course / Timeframe selects in `DrawerSidebar`.\n\nOut of scope (pre-existing staleness):\n- `SidebarPom.workspaceButtons`, `switchToWorkspace`, `deleteWorkspace`,\n  etc. still point at the aside, but `WorkspaceSwitcher` has lived in\n  TopBar for a while. Journey tests depend on these — left as-is; worth\n  a separate cleanup.\n\nTest plan:\n- `pnpm test` — 281/281 passing\n- `tsc` clean on new code\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqG1pECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD5EQAIQaoa0kJVBXQd3M4VtDB0LW\nCNrH/DjuBV/qBdrZkJCyX1GHKqPfWZZRYEdX46CKVh13onLlXGo7cGd9DaJdxIQy\nHuI/KI7P2QmBBvH0RzYSzg/VxALY16ka1el7M/JDeSPn2kvcwkVAk+9GbdE+/gAn\nu+/srYj4lfpdGb2lI+DM4ueY148U15qINqHJwBmeIJZkcnYg9y1ug0u/DspYF2JZ\n65Dott6aEYdT8eHDa/nEKkusod+emTKL0MT1zx8iL/Unq8E0sMBjnvqqZG6RnNyU\nH7rtpHAMSA+5qzaYdgfn9c7CVtrJfqGkNdhtU6U+HStBz2tD7jhU/ekbcUic2Az3\njuxT+aHAaUip3wDIjsEmLd8aI6A1Ffz7T0Jk1zNvPB9hHpg+lEJ0QX/HTNRk4Alu\nD+slk2Y2sBvfVI6e4CvL1wQC5ST0kNR8lmkLNIkGzpcHXcKcdF21D/dUAFW/KDs3\ny5BwPmobbTmAvTB4CNYba5sqLcC1y02NldUS/90+Trtc09PZiJp254ZRx60QaIpe\ny40/WbeMtp/mUEDxzmdafSVD/k3agPwHuT9qSGDn9dJrC4sVCiCGKv0XOsaXtDiZ\nGq5C8Y5TPj7HE/e1lp+5/hdrmfFY4aK2YbR4iHja48TqWzVSQG4PjVOBD3ZREUz4\nwH6jXKv4btmMh132sRLx\n=JQvB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-30T21:44:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9","node_id":"C_kwDOSFtkOtoAKDdhNWRhNDdkZDVjNjA4ZjI4OTI2YzAwNjNmNDM0MWZkZjA4YjA1Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commit/8d501b24db54a53d38a92227f4a97b253e43493e","sha":"8d501b24db54a53d38a92227f4a97b253e43493e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/8d501b24db54a53d38a92227f4a97b253e43493e"}],"sha":"7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/7a5da47dd5c608f28926c0063f4341fdf08b05f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31850876?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ed-Barnes937","id":31850876,"login":"Ed-Barnes937","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUwODc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ed-Barnes937","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/commits/8d501b24db54a53d38a92227f4a97b253e43493e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:43:41Z","email":"Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com","name":"Ed Barnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:43:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scope): drive sidebar pickers from manifest, add per-panel target picker (#46)\n\nSecond of three PRs from the workspace-scope rethink. Phase 3 — the UI\ncatches up to the contract introduced in PR 1.\n\nSidebar / TopBar:\n- `ScopeEditor` becomes dynamic. It renders only the pickers whose dims are\n  declared by at least one lens currently in the workspace\n  (`manifest.filters` union).\n- The whole Scope section is hidden when no lens declares any filter dim.\n  In Lecture now renders no Scope section; Evening Review and Exam Prep\n  render Course + Timeframe.\n- Drop the Recording dropdown and the \"New Recording\" button. Per-panel\n  target replaces them.\n- TopBar `useScopeSummary` drops the `recording` branch and returns null\n  when no filters are active; the chip is hidden in that case.\n\nPer-panel target picker:\n- New `LensProps.onConfigChange(patch)` callback; the shell wires it to a\n  new server mutation `workspaces.updatePanelConfig` (shallow-merges into\n  the panel''s persisted `config`).\n- New shared-ui `<RecordingPicker>` (presentational, takes recordings list\n  as a prop so shared-ui stays dependency-free).\n- Audio-capture and Transcript render the picker at the top of their UI.\n  Connections is `category: ''view''`; its `config.recordingId` stays static\n  for now (see PR description for trade-off).\n\nTest plan:\n- `pnpm test` — 281/281 passing\n- Playwright CT for touched packages — 77/77 passing\n- `tsc` clean on new code\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"522b607dee5b22700ab1ef075c971fc2fde6fad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/trees/522b607dee5b22700ab1ef075c971fc2fde6fad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ed-Barnes937/malleable-pls-poc/git/commits/8d501b24db54a53d38a92227f4a97b253e43493e","verification":{"payload":"tree 522b607dee5b22700ab1ef075c971fc2fde6fad2\nparent 22e985fedddf798f88e310de69454176911345db\nauthor Ed Barnes <Ed.Barnes937@gmail.com> 1780177421 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780177421 +0100\n\nfeat(scope): drive sidebar pickers from manifest, add per-panel target picker (#46)\n\nSecond of three PRs from the workspace-scope rethink. Phase 3 — the UI\ncatches up to the contract introduced in PR 1.\n\nSidebar / TopBar:\n- `ScopeEditor` becomes dynamic. It renders only the pickers whose dims are\n  declared by at least one lens currently in the workspace\n  (`manifest.filters` union).\n- The whole Scope section is hidden when no lens declares any filter dim.\n  In Lecture now renders no Scope section; Evening Review and Exam Prep\n  render Course + Timeframe.\n- Drop the Recording dropdown and the \"New Recording\" button. Per-panel\n  target replaces them.\n- TopBar `useScopeSummary` drops the `recording` branch and returns null\n  when no filters are active; the chip is hidden in that case.\n\nPer-panel target picker:\n- New `LensProps.onConfigChange(patch)` callback; the shell wires it to a\n  new server mutation `workspaces.updatePanelConfig` (shallow-merges into\n  the panel''s persisted `config`).\n- New shared-ui `<RecordingPicker>` (presentational, takes recordings list\n  as a prop so shared-ui stays dependency-free).\n- Audio-capture and Transcript render the picker at the top of their UI.\n  Connections is `category: ''view''`; its `config.recordingId` stays static\n  for now (see PR description for trade-off).\n\nTest plan:\n- `pnpm test` — 281/281 passing\n- Playwright CT for touched packages — 77/77 passing\n- `tsc` clean on new code\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqG1oNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1kQQAENLJjPD+x4pvuhf0qjFGud+\nLYqu2YDA90Nxdl4CBl3C6PfUS56aVbxbfBoYPneGQzzVAYLQyyC+wQvi0/Y/dlzm\nlteDbCTeUGU6VSsBTqpQAi7TE8iggT6tNp4feDlSjp1miYz3tcmbjH/ibweQ5aHh\nbcrLC1tbX6RVXKkPEqAk7+cAq1drC0zGgDuD+m+kotLKCQku9VKojOzGf6grcM3h\nlW94Ru1jqUR7o+i0L55n23ifClzoylD2LqIiLeBlGX0p4+Rxnj5+aOICOVaYu81J\n7+QOJsZO12RVFKVFC+tdQ1rVf/hd/lTlM+ze7NJi+azZdrB1qvCm/UL